    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Expression-of-Interest---Teaching-Associate--School-of-Computing_R000023452": {
      "title": "Expression of Interest – Teaching Associate, School of Computing",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-05-28\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPRIMARY DETAIL DISCOVER, CREATE, INNOVATE  The Faculty of Science and Engineering at Macquarie University delivers quality education to enable our students to reach their full potential, and work with our communities to discover, create and innovate with sustainability at our core.   THE ROLE  The School of Computing is inviting expressions of interest for inclusion within our casual academic pool for 2026.   For your application to be considered for Session 2 2026, please register your Expression of Interest (EOI) by Friday 12th June 2026 by uploading your relevant qualifications and requested details via the Workday application process. The School of Computing offers a range of undergraduate and postgraduate units to students completing courses in the Faculty of Science and Engineering, as well as service and elective units to students from across the campus. We employ casual academic staff to support our teaching of these courses.   We are currently inviting Expressions of interest (EOIs) from appropriately qualified individuals who demonstrate the following skills, qualifications, and experience.   ESSENTIAL CRITERIA   Completed Bachelor and/or Master’s degree in Computing, or a closely related discipline.  Sufficient discipline-specific knowledge  An understanding and appreciation of scholarly teaching  Excellent communication skills  Proven ability to interact effectively with students, staff and the community     TO APPLY  All interested applicants are required to upload a copy of their CV , copy of degree / testamur and a cover letter addressing the above criteria as part of the EOI process.  To assist in the review process, please complete this survey Qualtrics Survey | Qualtrics Experience Management (this survey is compulsory)   After initial review, applicants will be asked to prepare a short video to demonstrate their teaching style. If you are already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health): Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs.  If you are NOT currently part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health): click the 'Apply' button.  *Please note that this position is not available for visa sponsorship and the successful applicant must have work rights in Australia*   Position Enquiries: Elizabeth Bignucolo, Sessional Academic Staff Coordinator  at elizabeth.bignucolo@mq.edu.au Applications Close: Thursday, 31st of December 2026 11:59 pm (AEST) We reserve the right to progress or decline an application prior to the application closing date. If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 31/12/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Swimming-Coach_R000024487": {
      "title": "Swimming Coach",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-14\nPosted: Posted Today\nPart time\n\nCoach swimmers of all levels at MUSAC, delivering training, stroke correction, and competition prep in a dynamic, inclusive university squad program. THE ROLE Campus Life is currently seeking casual swimming coaches to join the Macquarie University Sports and Aquatics Centre (MUSAC) team. Reporting to the Head Coach, the casual swimming coaches will be responsible for delivering face to face training sessions in both competitive and recreational streams within the MQU Squad program. Duties include: Coach and develop swimmers from the Junior Development phase through to Senior Competition phase within the MQU Squad program Develop and implement seasonal training plans, providing coaching and advice on technical stroke correction and competition-based performance training plans Provide direction to swimmers of all abilities, adapting and modifying stroke models to suit varying abilities Attend and coach at MQU Club races, internal and external competitions In consultation with the Head Coach, plan and coordinate the running of MQU internal Club racing opportunities. In collaboration with the Head Coach and the coaching team, implement student retention activities Consult with Head Coach to assist and provide feedback within the squad program via the use of CRM system, for continued growth and improvement of the squad program Coach School Holiday Squad Programs Maintain accurate records on athletes/swimmers’ progression within the program Completion of administration duties including parent enquiries & parent feedback on student progression ABOUT US Macquarie University Sport and Aquatic Centre (MUSAC) is a multi-purpose venue. Located at Wallumattagal Campus, North Ryde, our facility includes a 6-lane heated indoor pool, and an 8-lane outdoor heated Olympic-sized swimming pool. The coaching team provides coaching and direction in best practice and techniques for competitive swimmers of all ages. At Campus Life we believe in a diverse, robust, and supportive work environment. We know our capacity to drive progressive change and offer excellent programs and services is increased when our team has a diversity of backgrounds and experience. We are committed to our people; we embrace diversity and welcome our people just as they are. Our Benefits Complementary Macquarie University Sport & Aquatic Centre gym access  Access to U @ MQ's VIP loyalty program Access to our staff wellbeing program and staff support services   Access to discounted corporate health insurance and employee flu shot program  ABOUT YOU You have a customer centric mindset combined with demonstrated experience teaching and coaching within the aquatics industry. You have the ability to work well in a team environment, as well as the initiative to work independently. In addition, you meet the following criteria: Hold Australian Swim Coach License from Swimming Australia as minimum Demonstrated experience coaching in a competitive/ development squad environment Possesses experience of competitive coaching of Metropolitan/Country level athletes and above Ability to develop and nurture swimmers of all abilities with diverse backgrounds Work hours will vary throughout the competition season. Must be available to work on a rotating roster seven (7) days per week. This role requires a NSW Working with Children Check, current First Aid and CPR certificates. TO APPLY If you want to work in a team of enthusiastic and like-minded people, whose passion is coaching swimmers of all abilities, in an encouraging and nurturing environment, please submit your CV and cover letter addressing your suitability for the role. For a position description or role-specific queries, please contact Tatiana Heavener on (02) 9850 1955 / swimming@mq.edu.au If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 11/10/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Enterprise-Architect--Applications-_R000023696": {
      "title": "Enterprise Architect (Applications)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-11\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCompetitive salary, commensurate   with skills and   experience​ plus 17% superannuation and annual leave loading 2-year fixed-term appointment | Hybrid working arrangement (3 days in the office per week) Macquarie University, Wallumattagal Campus, North Ryde Macquarie University Information Technology is hiring an experienced Enterprise Architect to provide strategic architectural leadership across some of the University's most complex and strategically significant application domains, including engagement, student, research and enabling applications such as finance, HR and facilities. This is a pivotal role at the heart of our digital transformation. You will act as a critical control point across high-value technology initiatives, helping the University make sound technology and investment decisions that align with institutional strategy, improve customer experiences and reduce duplication and complexity. Working across portfolios and functions, you will help shape future-state architecture and guide a pragmatic, value-driven transition from current to target state. If you are looking to apply your enterprise architecture expertise in an environment where your work has genuine, University-wide reach, this is an amazing opportunity to make a meaningful contribution. About the Role Reporting to the Director, IT Architecture, you will provide enterprise-wide architectural leadership, governance and expert advice to ensure the University's technology investments, platforms, capabilities and roadmaps align with institutional strategy, operational priorities and target customer experiences. Your key accountabilities will include: Providing enterprise-wide architectural leadership to guide technology direction, simplify complexity and align with organisational strategy and priorities. Defining, maintaining and communicating the enterprise architecture vision, principles, standards and roadmaps aligned to organisational strategy and target experiences. Developing and maintaining current-state, target-state and transition architectures, including capability models and strategic roadmaps, using an evidence-based approach. Providing architecture governance and assurance for major programs, projects, products, procurements and technology investments, and reviewing and endorsing solution architectures. Contributing to architecture governance boards and design authorities, handling exceptions, risks and technical debt in a controlled and transparent manner. Identifying opportunities to rationalise, modernise and optimise the technology landscape to improve value, reduce duplication and manage lifecycle costs, while ensuring decisions incorporate security, privacy, compliance, resilience and sustainability requirements. Building working relationships across IT and service units, and guiding solution architects, domain architects and technical leaders to uplift architecture capability and consistency of practice. About Us Macquarie University Information Technology (IT) supports the University's mission through the delivery of reliable, contemporary and strategically aligned digital services and technology capabilities. We have a service ethos and a commitment to collaboration, innovation and continuous improvement, working through trusted partnerships with stakeholders across the organisation to enable digital transformation, drive service improvements and deliver exceptional experiences. Within IT, the Architecture team provides advice, governance, standards and strategic direction across the University's digital landscape. About You (Selection Criteria ) You are an accomplished enterprise architect who brings significant expertise, strategic insight and the proven capability to influence technology direction across a complex organisational environment. You combine commercial, technical and stakeholder capabilities with a track record of aligning architecture practice to business strategy and transformation outcomes. Tertiary qualifications in a related discipline, or equivalent knowledge, skills and experience, with a demonstrated commitment to ongoing professional development. Extensive experience in enterprise architecture or senior architecture roles within large, complex organisations, including advising on major technology investments, transformation initiatives and enterprise-wide change programs that weigh business value, risk, cost, complexity and delivery feasibility. Knowledge of enterprise architecture disciplines, frameworks, governance and strategic planning processes (TOGAF certification or training is highly regarded), with the proven capability to translate business needs into architecture direction, standards and actionable roadmaps. Broad knowledge across enterprise application, cloud, data, integration, business process design, customer journey mapping and operating models to enable service and experience improvements. Well-developed problem-solving capability for architectural analysis across a complex technology landscape, including assessing current state, defining target state and identifying patterns, dependencies, risks and opportunities. Excellent stakeholder engagement and influencing skills, with the proven capability to build alignment and achieve outcomes across diverse stakeholder groups with competing priorities, and to clearly articulate complex concepts to technical and non-technical audiences. Experience in architecture governance and assurance, and the capability to guide architects, technical leaders and project teams to improve architecture maturity and consistency of practice; an understanding of the higher education sector or similarly complex multi-stakeholder environments is desirable. How to Apply To be considered, please apply online with your CV and a cover letter outlining how your experience aligns with the selection criteria (above). Applications Close Applications for this role will close on 25th September at 11.59 PM AEST. Why Join Us? Macquarie is a university engaged with the real and often complex problems and opportunities that define our lives. Since our foundation over 60 years ago, we have aspired to be a different type of university. Over the years, we have grown to become the centre of a vibrant local and global community. Connect with us today . We rank amongst the top employers in the Australian Workplace Employers Index. Explore the fantastic benefits available to you when you become part of the team at Macquarie University. Flexible, hybrid work arrangements 17% Superannuation Subsidised onsite parking options Extensive training and professional development programs Onsite childcare facilities to support working parents Onsite vacation care during school holidays Discounted health insurance Subsidised membership at our Sport & Aquatic Centre Access to an Employee Assistance Program for free and confidential support Convenient onsite GP, imaging, and physiotherapy clinics Pre-Employment Checks Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity. Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for. Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University. If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 25/09/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Student-Administrator_R000024468": {
      "title": "Student Administrator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-11\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAn opportunity exists for an enthusiastic, proactive administrator with strong attention to detail and excellent organisational skills to join our collaborative, fast-paced Student Administration team on campus. - Salary Package: $88,670 – $100,815 (HEW 5) p.a, plus 17% employer's superannuation and annual leave loading - Appointment Type: 2 full-time (35 hours per week), continuing appointment - Location: Macquarie University, Wallumattagal Campus (North Ryde) THE ROLE The Student Administration team serves as a crucial link between the academic teams, professional staff, and central university services, providing high-quality administrative support to current and prospective students and staff. As a Student Administrator, you will play a vital role in delivering student administrative services for Macquarie University College. This varied role includes: Providing administrative support to Macquaire University College students and staff. Supporting student lifecycle processes, including enrolment, articulation, progression, result updates, and completion activities. Responding to high volumes of student enquiries and providing advice on relevant policies, procedures, and program requirements in a timely manner. Maintaining accurate student records and processing transactions across multiple student management systems. Administering Special Consideration applications and coordinating follow-up actions. Scheduling and managing supplementary assessment sessions, Monitoring attendance, academic progression, and data quality to support compliance requirements and student success. Developing and enhancing student communications, templates, and operational procedures. Liaising regularly with the College and University stakeholders to support positive student outcomes. Identifying opportunities to improve administrative efficiencies, reduce processing delays, and maintain service quality during peak periods. Contributing to the continuous improvement of administrative systems, processes and procedures. Supporting positive culture within, across and beyond College teams by building and supporting respectful relationships with key stakeholders. ABOUT US Macquarie University College is wholly owned and operated by Macquaire University and provides students with an alternative pathway to a range of Macquarie University's undergraduate and postgraduate degrees by using our accelerated learning model. The College offers Diploma of Arts Media and Communications , Diploma of Business , Diploma of Business Analytics , Diploma of Commerce , Diploma of Engineering , Diploma of Information Technology , Diploma of Marketing & Media , Standard Foundation and Intensive Program , Masters Qualifying Program (Accelerated) and Masters Qualifying Program (Standard) , and a fee-free program called UniReady , launched in late 2025. We also deliver a suite of ELICOS (English language) programs, and non-award language programs and services including study tours, teacher training and the PTE Academic test centre. ABOUT YOU As the successful candidate, you will be capable of establishing effective working relationships with staff at all levels. You will have the confidence and skills to problem-solve, learn new systems and processes as needed, and actively engage in the face-to-face everyday workings of the College. You will have excellent time management skills, high levels of accuracy and attention to detail, and be highly skilled in the use of the Microsoft suite of products. You will be familiar with learning and teaching organisations and systems, and will be able to maintain confidentiality, discretion, and professionalism at all times. To Apply To be considered for this position, please apply online by submitting your CV and a separate (2-page maximum) cover letter that demonstrates how you meet the following selection criteria: Degree and/or equivalent experience in business administration or similar discipline, Demonstrated organisational and office administration skills in fast-paced, high-volume environment, Excellent customer service skills, with the ability to respond to a high volume of enquiries in a professional and timely manner, Proven ability to maintain confidentiality and handle sensitive information appropriately, Strong attention to detail and demonstrated experience maintaining accurate records and processing transactions across systems, Excellence in managing multiple priorities and meeting deadlines, Advanced computer proficiency including MS Office, and experience working with student management systems or similar databases Knowledge of the Australian higher education sector, Foundation Programs and ELICOS sectors and the regulatory environment is desirable. Note: It is expected that you will be available to work on campus most days of the week. *** This role requires a Police Check and applicants are preferred to hold a current Working with Children Check (WWCC) or be willing to obtain one. For enquiries about the role, please contact Mandy Lam, Student Administration Team Leader at mandy.lam@mq.edu.au Applications close:  Sunday, 27 September 2026 at 11:59 p.m. (AEST) Please Note: Interviews are expected to be conducted face-to-face on Thursday, 8 October & Friday, 9 October. Please ensure you are available on both days, as the interview may be scheduled on either date. This position is not available for visa sponsorship, and the successful applicant must have valid work rights in Australia. Pre-Employment Checks Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity. Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for. Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University. Why Join Us? We rank amongst the top employers in the Australian Workplace Employers Index. Explore the fantastic benefits available to you when you become part of the team at Macquarie University. Our prime location is just a short walk from Macquarie University Metro Station and Macquarie Shopping Centre. Enjoy the benefits of working at a campus that offers: 17% Superannuation Subsidised onsite parking options Flexible working options Training and professional development Onsite childcare facilities Discounted health insurance (Medibank) Onsite vacation care Employee Assistance Program Subsidised membership at the Sport & Aquatic Centre Onsite GP, imaging & physio clinics If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 27/09/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Recruitment-Consultant--Undergraduates_R000024431": {
      "title": "Undergraduate Recruitment Consultant",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-11\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n· Annual base salary from $114,992 - $124, 676 per annum (HEW Level 7) plus 17% superannuation and annual leave loading · Full-time, continuing appointment · Based at Macquarie University, Wallumattagal Campus, North Ryde with hybrid working arrangements About the role Our Domestic Future Students team is seeking an experienced Recruitment Consultant to implement school recruitment strategies and activities that contribute to the University’s commencing undergraduate enrolment goals. As a Recruitment Consultant (Schools) you will be building and maintaining relationships with schools to connect prospective students with the opportunities that a Macquarie University education can offer. Reporting to the Manager, Undergraduate Future Students (Schools), you will help design and deliver a program of events and initiatives for high school students and their influencers. Your responsibilities will include: In partnership with the Manager, planning, delivering and continuously improving a program of events and initiatives for high school students, current school-leavers and their influencers, and providing support at student recruitment events. Building strong collaborative relationships with key schools to increase participation in recruitment activities and drive domestic undergraduate applications that contribute to enrolment goals. Representing the University and coordinating its contribution to student recruitment events, initiatives and programs. Providing information to prospective undergraduate students, parents and school staff on the University's courses, admissions and entry criteria. Contributing to data analysis, reporting and presentations that surface insights and opportunities for growth, including for senior management. Developing and maintaining presentation decks and campus tour content for prospective students and their influencers. Contributing to knowledge development of Student Ambassadors to support the  delivery of recruitment and promotional activities. About Us The Future Students team coordinates the international and domestic recruitment strategy of the University and helps Faculties and other portfolios with their student recruitment activities, events, collaboration and engagement. Working across the institution, the team generates significant value for the University and helps maintain a well-established recruitment and partnership network. This role sits within the People and Operations portfolio, led by the Deputy Vice-Chancellor, People and Operations. About You You are a relationship-focused professional who enjoys engaging with a wide range of people and thrives in a varied, event-based environment. You bring sound planning skills, an eye for detail and experience in higher education and the student journey. You are comfortable using data to shape activities and enjoy seeing the results of your work reflected in growing engagement. To Apply To be considered for this position, please apply online and attach your resume and a separate cover letter that addresses how you meet the below selection criteria (maximum 2 pages): Degree and/or equivalent extensive experience in business, marketing or related discipline. Understanding of the secondary and higher education sector and the end-to-end prospective undergraduate student journey. Knowledge of project management principles and sales strategies, with experience developing and delivering strategies, campaigns and initiatives that meet goals. Experience coordinating events and activities and guiding staff, along with managing multiple projects to objectives and timelines. Experience collating and analysing data to inform strategies, with a focus on continuous improvement. A record of building and managing effective relationships with internal and external stakeholders, including the ability to engage and inform. Excellent interpersonal and communication (written and verbal) skills, with strong attention to detail and time management, and the ability to present to a wide range of audiences. ***Please note: A Working with Children Check and criminal check is required for this role. Work hours may vary from time to time to accommodate business needs. Applications Close: 11.59pm, Monday, 21 September 2026 For a confidential conversation about the role please contact Jenny Rickard, Manager, Undergraduate Future Students (Schools) at jenny.rickard@mq.edu.au . We reserve the right to progress or decline applications prior to the closing date, including closing the advertisement earlier than advertised. Why join us? Macquarie is a university engaged with the real and often complex problems and opportunities that define our lives. Since our foundation over 60 years ago, we have aspired to be a different type of university. Over the years, we have grown to become the centre of a vibrant local and global community. Connect with us today. We rank amongst the top employers in the Australian Workplace Employers Index. Explore the fantastic benefits available to you when you become part of the team at Macquarie University. Flexible, hybrid work arrangements 17% Superannuation Subsidised onsite parking options Extensive training and professional development programs Onsite childcare facilities to support working parents Onsite vacation care during school holidays Discounted health insurance Subsidised membership at our Sport & Aquatic Centre Access to an Employee Assistance Program for free and confidential support Convenient onsite GP, imaging, and physiotherapy clinics Pre-Employment Checks Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity. Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for. Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University. If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 10/09/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Senior-Student-Administration-Officer_R000024395-1": {
      "title": "Senior Student Administration Officer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-11\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nDeliver exceptional student experiences, apply your specialist knowledge, and help shape services that matter. · Salary Package: From $102,136 (HEW 6) per annum, plus 17% superannuation and annual leave loading · Appointment type: Full-time, fixed term appointment until December 2027 · Location: Macquarie University, Wallumattagal Campus, North Ryde Every student journey is shaped by the quality of support they receive along the way. In this role within Student Shared Services, you will be at the heart of that experience, providing specialised and escalated administration and advisory services to international and domestic students across a range of teams. This is an opportunity to bring your expertise in student administration to a collaborative, high-performing environment where accuracy, care and continuous improvement come together. You will handle complex enquiries, apply your knowledge of policies and legislation, and help ensure our students receive timely, reliable and quality-assured service at every touchpoint. If you enjoy solving complex queries, working with a range of systems, and partnering with colleagues to improve how we do things, we would be glad to hear from you. About the Role   Reporting within Student Shared Services, you will provide higher-level and escalated student administration, advisory and transactional services. Your day-to-day contributions will include:   Providing specialised advice, customer service and complex transactional support to international and domestic students.   Applying and sharing specialist knowledge of student administration policies, procedures, standards and legislation.   Undertaking complex transactional processing across a range of student administration systems, ensuring timely , accurate and quality-assured data.   Reviewing, analysing, assessing and following up on complex or specialised student queries in line with established policies and the University's terms and conditions.   Executing and, where needed, escalating complex enquiries by liaising with multiple internal stakeholders to reach effective resolutions.   Contributing to projects and initiatives that improve student services, processes and systems, including providing feedback on work practices.   Completing regular quality assurance of work and developing and maintaining reporting on student administration services and transactions.   Monitoring your own workload to prioritise tasks, meet targets and timelines, and help deliver quality individual and team outcomes.   Building and maintaining relationships with internal and external stakeholders and complying with relevant EEO and WHS regulations.   About Us   Macquarie is a university engaged with the real and often complex problems and opportunities that define our lives. Since our foundation in 1964, we have aspired to be a different type of university. Over the years, we have grown to become the centre of a vibrant local and global community. Connect with us today .     Student Shared Services plays a vital part in this mission, providing specialised administration and advisory services that support our students succeed throughout their journey with us from offer through to completion. With a strong focus on service excellence and the student experience, Student Shared Services works collaboratively across the University to deliver efficient, responsive and student-centred services.     The Student Enrolments team within Student Shared Services supports key enrolment-related processes and activities across the student lifecycle. Working closely with students and stakeholders across the University , the team helps ensure enrolment services are delivered accurately, efficiently , and in accordance with University policies and procedures.   About You   You are an experienced student administration or customer service professional who brings specialist knowledge, attention to detail and a genuine focus on service quality. You enjoy navigating complex queries, working across systems, and helping improve the way services are delivered. You bring an understanding of the higher education environment and work effectively alongside a range of colleagues and stakeholders.   Selection Criteria   Degree or equivalent experience in customer service, business, business systems or a related discipline.   Knowledge of student customer service and/or administration processes and associated policies.   Experience providing specialised transactional support to students.   A clear customer service focus and the ability to work and communicate effectively with others.   Experience contributing to continuous service improvement and transformation initiatives.   Time management and organisational skills, with experience coordinating and delivering on competing deadlines.   Experience managing, analysing and reporting on data and complex business processes.   ***  Appointment to this role will be subject to successful completion of a criminal history check.   How to Apply   To be considered for this position , please apply online with your CV and a cover letter outlining how your experience meets the selection criteria (above).   Applications Close: Sunday 20 September 2026 at 11:59 p.m. (AEST)   We reserve the right to progress or decline an application prior to the application closing date.   For enquiries about the role , please contact Hina Ali, Enrolment Team Leader at hina.ali@mq.edu.au .   Pre-Employment Checks   Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity. Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for.   Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University.    If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 20/09/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Lecturer-in-Engineering--Research-and-Teaching-_R000024191": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Engineering (Research and Teaching)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-11\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n- Salary package:  $127,138 - $150,425 (Level B.1 – B.6) plus 17% employer's superannuation contribution and annual leave loading. - Three full-time, continuing roles - Based at Macquarie University, Wallumattagal Campus, North Ryde The School of Engineering is seeking three dynamic, early-to-mid-career rising stars to join us as Lecturers (Level B) . We have the flexibility to appoint across Civil, Mechanical and Mechatronic Engineering.  We are looking for outstanding academics who bridge the gap between engineering theory and practical execution. While academic rigor is essential, we are explicitly looking for individuals who know how to build engineering artifacts. You possess strong practical engineering skills, a passion for prototyping, design, or implementation, and the ability to inspire students through hands-on, project-based education. In these roles, you will contribute to our rapidly growing undergraduate and postgraduate programs, supervise Higher Degree by Research (HDR) students, and develop an impactful, independent research profile that translates innovative ideas into tangible, real-world solutions. These roles are full-time, continuing (tenure-track) positions, based at our Wallumattagal (North Ryde) Campus in Sydney. About Us The School of Engineering at Macquarie University is rapidly expanding the capacity and impact of its research and education frameworks. As a comprehensive school, our expertise spans civil, environmental, mechanical, mechatronic, biomedical, electrical, and electronic engineering. This year, we established our operations in a brand-new, $150 million education and research precinct: the Engineering Innovation Building. This facility features state-of-the-art spaces designed specifically for immersive, team-based design and manufacturing projects, alongside specialist laboratories hosting our highly ranked research groups. As part of the Faculty of Science and Engineering (FSE), we nurture the next generation of technology innovators, supporting nearly 9,000 students across our programs. Our research and teaching directly address the critical challenges faced by global society—including infrastructure resilience, autonomous systems, future materials, and sustainable energy. To Apply To be considered for this position, candidates must submit a copy of their curriculum vitae alongside a statement of no more than five pages addressing the selection criteria outlined below. Essential criteria (Lecturer Level B) To be successful, candidates will need to demonstrate their capability across the following areas: A PhD in Civil, Mechanical, Mechatronic, or a closely related engineering discipline. Demonstrated hands-on engineering skills with a track record of physical prototyping, experimental system design, field testing, or practical project execution. Evidence of capability to design and deliver engaging, high-quality, project-led learning experiences that develop both the technical and practical competencies of engineering students. A developing or established track record of quality publications and a clear trajectory for securing external research funding or industry partnerships. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to collaborate effectively across disciplinary boundaries and work with industry partners. The Faculty of Science and Engineering at Macquarie University has a goal to increase the engagement of women, Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people from diverse backgrounds in STEMM roles. Applications are considered holistically, and candidates are encouraged to apply even if their experience does not meet each individual selection criterion. *This position requires a criminal history and qualifications check. Applications Close: Sunday 18th of October at 11:59pm (AEST). We reserve the right to progress or decline an application prior to the application closing date. For enquiries, or a confidential conversation about the role please contact Professor Gordon Wyeth, Dean of School of Engineering: fse.eng-dean@mq.edu.au . Pre-Employment Checks Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity. Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for.  Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University. If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 18/10/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Associate-Professor-of-Engineering_R000024150": {
      "title": "Associate Professor of Engineering",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-11\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n- Salary package:  $186,433 - $205,067 (Level D.1 – D.4) plus 17% employer's superannuation contribution and annual leave loading. - Full-time, continuing role - Based at Macquarie University, Wallumattagal Campus, North Ryde About the Role The School of Engineering invites applications for an Associate Professor in Civil Engineering (Teaching and Research) with a specialization in Transport Engineering . In this role, you will deliver high-quality undergraduate and postgraduate education, supervise Higher Degree by Research (HDR) students, secure competitive research funding, and strengthen Macquarie University’s strategic connections within the transport industry. The successful applicant will have a proven track record of creating engaging learning experiences for students and driving real-world impact through their research. We are seeking candidates with expertise in making transportation systems efficient, reliable, affordable, and sustainable. Areas of particular interest include network planning and modelling, safety, public transport analysis, and environmental modelling. This is a full-time, continuing (tenure-track) position based at our Wallumattagal (North Ryde) Campus in Sydney. About Us The School of Engineering at Macquarie University is rapidly expanding the capacity and impact of its research and education frameworks. As a comprehensive school, our expertise spans civil, environmental, mechanical, mechatronic, biomedical, electrical, and electronic engineering. This year, we established our operations in a brand-new, $150 million education and research precinct: the Engineering Innovation Building. This facility features state-of-the-art spaces designed specifically for project- and team-based learning, alongside specialist laboratories hosting our highly ranked research groups. As part of the Faculty of Science and Engineering (FSE), we nurture the next generation of technology innovators, supporting nearly 9,000 students across our programs. Our research and teaching directly address the critical challenges faced by global society—including the changing environment, future materials, sustainable fuels, and biotechnology. To Apply To be considered for this position, candidates must submit a copy of their curriculum vitae alongside a statement of no more than five pages addressing the selection criteria outlined below. Essential criteria for appointment at Associate Professor (Level D) A PhD in Civil Engineering, Transport Engineering, or a closely related discipline. A demonstrated and growing national and international reputation for academic excellence, evidenced by independent, innovative, and sustained contributions to research and education in transport engineering. Demonstrated ability to lead, design, and deliver high-quality curriculum and transformative teaching and learning experiences, with a track record of high student satisfaction and engagement. Proven leadership in securing and managing competitive research grants (e.g., ARC) and/or industry-funded projects, leading to high-impact publications and tangible socio-economic or policy outcomes. A sustained track record of successful Higher Degree Research (HDR) supervision to completion, and a commitment to mentoring candidates toward successful academic or industry careers. Demonstrated leadership in contributing to a positive, collaborative, and inclusive workplace culture that values diversity of thought, equity, and the professional development of colleagues. Outstanding communication, negotiation, and interpersonal skills, with a proven ability to build strategic partnerships and work effectively with internal institutional stakeholders and external industry or government partners. The Faculty of Science and Engineering at Macquarie University has a goal to increase the engagement of women, Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people from diverse backgrounds in STEMM roles. Applications are considered holistically, and candidates are encouraged to apply even if their experience does not meet each individual selection criterion. *This position requires a criminal history and qualifications check. Applications Close: Sunday 18th of October 2026 at 11:59pm (AEST). We welcome applications from international candidates. We reserve the right to progress or decline an application prior to the application closing date. For enquiries, or a confidential conversation about the role please contact Professor Gordon Wyeth, Dean of School of Engineering: fse.eng-dean@mq.edu.au Pre-Employment Checks  Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity. Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for.  Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University.  If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 18/10/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Postdoctoral-Research-Associate--Engineering-_R000024439": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate (Engineering)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-11\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n- Salary package:  $112,550 - $120,621 (A.6-A.8) per annum, plus 17% employer's superannuation contribution and annual leave loading. - Full-time, one-year fixed term role - Based at Macquarie University, Wallumattagal Campus, North Ryde The Role We are seeking a highly motivated and skilled research associate to contribute to a discovery project on upcycling waste plastics funded by the Australian Research Council. The successful candidate should have research experience in catalysis engineering and reactor system design. They will have excellent oral and written communication skills and ability to work in a team collaborating across disciplines. About You You will be an emerging researcher with strong experimental capability and demonstrated expertise in catalyst design, spectroscopy, and process optimization. You enjoy hands‑on laboratory work, iterative troubleshooting, and mentoring junior researchers. You are collaborative, organised, and committed to producing high‑quality scientific outcomes. About Us The School of Engineering  sits within the Faculty of Science and Engineering and is a diverse community of academics blazing new trails in the spirit of discovery, exploration and impact.  We are talented and knowledgeable engineers and form teams of innovators and creators with a passion for a strong desire to make an impact in research. To Apply To apply for this position, please apply online by submitting your CV and a separate cover letter (no more than 2 pages) that demonstrates how you meet the following selection criteria: PhD in Materials Engineering, Chemical Engineering, or a related discipline Demonstrated research expertise in catalyst design, spectroscopy, or process optimization Role-specific Enquiries: Professor Yijiao Jiang, yijiao.jiang@mq.edu.au Applications Close:  Friday 25th of September 2026 at 11:59pm (AEST) *** Applications will be reviewed as they are received, and we reserve the right to progress or decline an application prior to the application closing date. We also reserve the right to close the advertisement early if a sufficient number of qualified applicants is received. The Faculty of Science and Engineering at Macquarie University has a goal to increase the engagement of women, Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people from diverse backgrounds in STEMM roles. Applications are considered holistically, and candidates are encouraged to apply even if their experience does not meet each individual selection criterion. Why work at Macquarie We rank amongst the top employers in the Australian Workplace Employers Index, having recently earned a five-star rating in the QS World Rankings with the highest rating for employability. Our prime location, we are walking distance from Macquarie University Metro Station and Macquarie Shopping Centre.  Not only are we close, take a look at our benefits on offer:     17% Superannuation     Subsidised onsite parking options    Flexible working options    Training and professional development    Onsite childcare facilities    Discounted health insurance (Medibank)    Onsite vacation care    Employee Assistance Program    Subsidised membership at the Sport & Aquatic Centre   Onsite GP, imaging & physio clinics   Pre-Employment Checks Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity. Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for.  Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University.  If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 25/09/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Early-Childhood-Educator-Certificate-III-Qualified_R000024337": {
      "title": "Early Childhood Educator Certificate III Qualified",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-10\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNurture curiosity, spark a lifelong love of learning, and help shape the earliest years at a vibrant University campus. · Above-award salary + 12% superannuation · 2 full-time, continuing positions · Gumnut Cottage Child Care Centre, U@MQ Ltd — Macquarie University, Wallumattagal Campus, North Ryde Do you believe that the early years are a unique and valuable time in a child's life? At Gumnut Cottage Child Care Centre, one of Campus Life's early learning centres on Macquarie University's campus, you will play a meaningful part in delivering high-quality, play-based early education within a welcoming community. This is an opportunity to grow your career in an environment where your development is prioritised and your contribution is genuinely valued. About the Role We are looking for 2 full-time Certificate III qualified Educators to join the team at Gumnut Cottage Child Care Centre. Reporting to the Room Leader, you will be an advocate for children, champion quality early education, and value the relationships that make learning thrive. In return, you will enjoy an above-award salary, generous benefits, and a workplace built around care, respect, and shared purpose. As a Certificate III Educator, you will help create an inclusive, engaging educational program that puts the wellbeing and growth of every child first. Working alongside a large and diverse team, your day-to-day contributions will include: Contributing to the educational program, including maintaining developmental records. Interacting positively and respectfully with children and families. Working effectively and collaboratively within a large, diverse team. Maintaining a current understanding of the Early Years Learning Framework (EYLF) and National Quality Standards. Contributing to all diversity, equity, and inclusion activities. Engaging in ongoing professional development and continuous improvement. Following approved policies and procedures to help keep children safe (child protection, supervision, health and wellbeing). You will also enjoy a range of benefits designed to help you thrive, including: Education and professional development opportunities Paid lunch breaks with no requirement to remain on premises Paid staff meetings and generous release time Free access to the Macquarie University Sport & Aquatic Centre Additional paid concessional days Access to our staff wellbeing program, staff support services, and employee flu shot program Discounted corporate health insurance Rewards app to earn points on purchases at selected Campus Life outlets Subsidised onsite parking options Onsite vacation care during school holidays About Us U@MQ Ltd is a not-for-profit controlled entity of Macquarie University, known as Campus Life. Located at Macquarie University's Wallumattagal Campus, North Ryde, Campus Life operates four early learning centers providing high-quality education to children from six weeks of age, along with a vacation care program for primary school–aged children. Our play-based educational and school holiday programs are built around encouraging a love of learning through curiosity, creativity, and innovation; building relationships with others, oneself, and the environment; fostering each child's dispositions for learning; prioritising children's wellbeing; and celebrating childhood as a unique and valuable time. At Gumnut Cottage, relationships are central to everything we do, and belonging is inclusive for all. You can read more in our Gumnut Cottage Philosophy . We have access to university spaces and facilities to support and enhance our programs and collaborate regularly with the University’s community, including the Macquarie School of Education. We are committed to the safety of children and our people. We embrace diversity, welcome our people just as they are, and prioritise professional development. At Campus Life, you will benefit from being part of a dynamic, committed and supportive team. About You You are an enthusiastic early childhood educator who believes in the value of quality early education and the relationships that underpin it. You bring a genuine commitment to children’s wellbeing, an inclusive and collaborative approach, and a desire to continue developing professionally. You will share our organisational values of Courage, Agility, Rigour, Empowerment and Support (CARES) and demonstrate these through your actions and interactions. Selection Criteria ACECQA-approved Certificate III in early childhood education Demonstrated experience working with children aged 0–5 years in a regulated early learning setting, Experience contributing to inclusive educational programs that support children’s learning, development and wellbeing, Sound understanding of the National Quality Framework, including the EYLF, National Law, Regulations, and child protection legislation, including responsibilities as a Mandatory Reporter, Ability to build positive, respectful and ethical relationships with children, families, colleagues and the broader community, Ability to actively supervise children and contribute to a safe, inclusive and engaging learning environment, and Strong communication, interpersonal and teamwork skills, with the ability to contribute positively within a large and diverse team. Qualifications & Specific Requirements (The following must be current or completed before commencement) First Aid, Asthma and Anaphylaxis qualification Working with Children Check Geccko child safety training qualification Food Handling training Current Child Protection training, including a recognised course code for CHCPRT025 – Identify and Report Children and Young People at Risk *** You must be legally entitled to work in Australia. How to Apply If being part of an inclusive, vibrant, team orientated organisation is something you are passionate about, we encourage you to apply. To be considered, please apply online. You do not need to submit a cover letter, but please be prepared to respond to questions at interview related to the Selection Criteria listed above. For general enquiries or a copy of the Position Description, please contact Tara Kelly, Gumnut Cottage, on 9850 7740, or TARA.KELLY@mq.edu.au . If you need any support or reasonable adjustments throughout this recruitment process, please let us know so we can provide the support you need. Applications Close: Sunday 27 September 2026 at 11:59 p.m. (AEST) We reserve the right to progress or decline an application prior to the application closing date. Pre-Employment Checks Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity. Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for. Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University. Child Safe Commitment Statement Campus Life is committed to the safety, wellbeing, and empowerment of all children and young people engaging in our programs, and to protecting them from foreseeable harm. We treat all allegations and complaints about the safety and wellbeing of children seriously, and we ensure that our staff, volunteers, and contractors understand their legal obligations to report child abuse and neglect to government authorities. Every Campus Life employee has a responsibility to understand the important and specific role they play, both individually and collectively, to keep the wellbeing and safety of all children and young people at the forefront of everything they do. If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 27/09/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Education-Support-Officer_R000024433-1": {
      "title": "Education Support Officer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-10\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nHelp shape the student journey, enable outstanding course delivery and make a real difference to learning experiences. · Salary Package: From $102,136 per annum (HEW Level 6.1), plus 17% superannuation and annual leave loading · Appointment Type: Full-time, fixed-term until 23 July 2027 (flexible work options available) · Macquarie University, Wallumattagal Campus, North Ryde Are you looking for a role where your organisational talents and knowledge of higher education can directly enhance the way students learn and thrive? As an Education Support Officer within Macquarie Business School, you will be a trusted point of contact for academic staff, helping to bring courses to life across their full lifecycle. Working as part of a welcoming Educational Services team, you will provide integrated advice and coordination that keeps course delivery running smoothly, from annual planning and assessment preparation through to result ratification and student enquiries. Your work will help create a seamless and rewarding experience for both staff and students. This is a wonderful opportunity to grow your career within a leading university, contribute to meaningful educational outcomes, and be part of a community that values your input and celebrates shared achievement. About the Role Reporting to the Course/Education Support Team Leader within Macquarie Business School, you will provide operational and administrative support that enhances the quality of course delivery and the student experience. Depending on the Business School’s needs, you may support a single course, a collection of courses, or a department. Key responsibilities include: Providing advice and support to Course Directors, Discipline Chairs, Heads of School or Department and Unit Convenors on all matters related to the delivery and administration of courses and units. Coordinating operational and administrative support across the lifecycle of a course to enhance delivery and the student experience. Contributing to and coordinating annual planning, communication of key milestones, and the development of resources such as Study Plans and Course Guides. Coordinating the preparation and delivery of assessments, along with moderation, result ratification, and grade administration. Delivering course-specific orientation and onboarding activities in partnership with the Faculty Student Experience team. Providing administrative and secretarial support for course-specific meetings, including industry advisory boards, and progressing actions arising. Advising timetabling teams to coordinate class registration and management, with a focus on course-level timetabling. Acting as a liaison point for teaching staff, including coordinating guest lecturers, external experts and sessional staff. Partnering across the University to identify and implement improvements to student administration processes, and to help resolve complex student lifecycle enquiries and cases. About Us Macquarie is a university engaged with the real and often complex problems and opportunities that define our lives. Since our foundation in 1964, we have aspired to be a different type of university. Over the years, we have grown to become the centre of a vibrant local and global community.  Connect with us today . Macquarie Business School is one of Australia's leading business schools, known for research-led teaching, strong industry connections, and a commitment to shaping capable, globally minded graduates. As part of this dynamic Faculty, our people work together to deliver an exceptional and forward-thinking educational experience. Within the Business School, the Education Services Team helps bring this commitment to life. The team provides integrated, high-quality support across the course lifecycle, working closely with academic staff to enable smooth course delivery and a seamless student journey. This role sits at the heart of that work. About You You are an organised and people-focused professional who enjoys enabling others to succeed. With sound knowledge of the higher education environment and a genuine service focus, you bring calm coordination to busy and varied workloads. You enjoy building effective working relationships across teams and helping to improve the way things are done. Selection Criteria A degree or tertiary qualification in a relevant field and/or equivalent relevant experience. Knowledge of tertiary education policies, processes, and course and unit governance structures. Experience providing advice and operational support relating to policies, course delivery and/or complex student services, preferably within a higher education environment. Strong customer service skills and the ability to build effective working relationships with academic staff, committees and other stakeholders. Experience developing annual planning documentation and project plans, providing high-quality administrative support, and using Microsoft Office and database management systems. Strong organisational and time-management skills, with the ability to coordinate competing priorities and meet deadlines. Experience analysing data and proactively developing and implementing administrative process improvements. Strong written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to draft papers, submissions and other professional documentation. Note: The successful candidate will be required to complete a police check prior to commencement. *** Applicants must hold valid Australian work rights for the duration of the appointment. How to Apply To be considered, please apply online with your CV and a cover letter outlining how your experience aligns with the selection criteria (above). Applications Close: Friday 25 September 2026, 11:59 p.m. (AEST) **We reserve the right to progress or decline an application prior to the application closing date. We also reserve the right to close the advertisement early if a sufficient number of qualified applicants is received. For enquiries about the role, please contact Prani Manandhar, Course / Education Support Team Leader at prani.manandhar@mq.edu.au . Why Join Us? We rank amongst the top employers in the Australian Workplace Employers Index. Explore the fantastic benefits available to you when you become part of the team at Macquarie University. Our prime location is just a short walk from Macquarie University Metro Station and Macquarie Shopping Centre. Enjoy the benefits of working at a campus that offers: 17% Superannuation Subsidised onsite parking options Flexible working options Training and professional development Onsite childcare facilities Discounted health insurance (Medibank) Onsite vacation care Employee Assistance Program Subsidised membership at the Sport & Aquatic Centre Onsite GP, imaging & physio clinics Pre-Employment Checks Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity. Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for. Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University. If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 09/09/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Member-Experience-Officer_R000024201": {
      "title": "Member Experience Officer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-10\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nAn exciting and fast-paced customer service role based in a busy gym that contributes to a great experience for our members. Our Member Experience team is a key function within our centre. As one of our Member Experience Officers you will be: Providing a consistent and high level of service to members and guests to drive acquisition and member retention. Responding to and actioning customer queries in-person, over the phone and via email. Executing acquisition and retention strategies and campaigns to sell memberships. Following established processes and procedures for memberships, point of sale transactions, cash handling, end-to-end venue hire bookings, and administration processes associated with the Centres operations and safety policy. Respond to member and guest feedback, providing constructive information to continuously improve outcomes that support a positive customer experience. About You To be successful in this role you will need: Proven experience in a front-line customer facing role. Demonstrated success in achieving sales targets, prioritising tasks, and meeting deadlines. A proven record of accomplishment in the area of customer experience and continuous improvement. Well-developed interpersonal and communication skills including the ability to work collaboratively and to establish, build and maintain respectful and ethical relationships with staff, students, and other key stakeholders. Excellent organisational and time management skills and attention to detail. Proficient skills in Microsoft Office applications, including database management. This role requires a criminal history check, First Aid and CPR certificate. Standard work hours will require you to be available on weekends, early mornings and evenings to meet the needs of the business. About Us Macquarie University Sport and Aquatic Centre (MUSAC) is a multi-purpose venue designed to help meet all the health, fitness and sporting needs of our members and guests. Our facilities include a 6-lane heated indoor pool, and an 8-lane outdoor heated Olympic-sized swimming pool. The centre features a fully equipped health club, group and virtual fitness classes, squash courts, gymnastics / aquatics programs and social sports. Macquarie University Sport Fields operates 7 days a week, our facilities include 5 professional playing fields which accommodates a variety of events, stadium lighting, canteen and BBQ areas, and four change rooms. Benefits: Complementary Macquarie University Sport & Aquatic Centre gym access Access to our staff wellbeing program and staff support services  Working on a vibrant parkland campus, with a huge variety of food & beverage outlets, and general practice & hospital amenities Access to discounted corporate health insurance and employee flu shot program Staff discounts at Campus Life operated hospitality outlets To Apply: If being part of an inclusive, vibrant, team orientated organisation is something you are passionate about we encourage you to apply.   In the first instance, general enquiries should be directed to Xavier Maniacara on 02 9850 1022, or via email xavier.maniacara@mq.edu.au . To be considered for this position, you must submit your CV and a cover letter addressing the listed criteria in the About You section via our online application portal. If you need any support or reasonable adjustments through this recruitment process, please let us know so we can provide the support you need. If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 20/09/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Sessional-Teaching-Academic---School-of-International-Studies--Global-Cultures-and-Languages---German-Language----Expression-of-Interest_R000023644": {
      "title": "Sessional Teaching Academic - School of International Studies (Global Cultures and Languages – German Language) - Expression of Interest",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-10\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nJob Description Summary Casual marking and tutoring opportunities (Semester 2, 2026 – 2028) German Language Macquarie University (North Ryde) location THE ROLE The School of International Studies is inviting Expressions of Interest (EOI) for inclusion within our casual academic pool from 2026-2028. If you are interested in being engaged as a casual teaching academic for German teaching at Macquarie University, please register your Expression of Interest and provide the requested details contained in the online Qualtrics Survey and Workday application process as detailed below. Currently we are looking to expand our pool to fill potential gaps in 2026, with more work opening up in 2027. The School of International Studies offers a range of undergraduate and postgraduate units to students completing courses within the Faculty of Arts, as well as offering elective Arts units to students from other faculties at Macquarie University and OUA. We are currently inviting Expressions of Interest from appropriately qualified individuals for inclusion within our appointable pool of casual academics to provide marking and tutoring support during the 2026 academic year.  For your application to be considered for this year, please register your Expression of Interest (EOI) via the online Qualtrics Survey and Workday application by July 19th. ESSENTIAL CRITERIA Fluency in German Experience teaching language at the tertiary level Excellent communication skills Proven ability to interact effectively with students, staff and the community TO APPLY All interested applicants are required to upload a copy of their CV, copy of degree / testamur and a cover letter addressing the above subject areas as part of the EOI process. To assist in the review process, please complete this survey (this survey is compulsory). If you are already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM): Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. If you are NOT currently part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM): click the 'Apply' button.   *Please note that this position is not available for visa sponsorship and the successful applicant must have work rights in Australia* Position Enquiries: Please email Dr. Wes Robertson ( wes.robertson@mq.edu.au ) for enquiries. We reserve the right to progress or decline an application prior to the application closing date. Pre-Employment Checks Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University. About Us Macquarie is a university engaged with the real and often complex problems and opportunities that define our lives. Celebrating its 60th year in 2024, it was established as a bold experiment in higher education and designed to break from educational traditions to work in tandem with industry. Institutionally we strive for the extraordinary by challenging convention and embracing different views. Our pioneering culture has encouraged and inspired students, staff and collaborators to break free from conventional thinking, and to actively shape the complex issues that define the future of humanity. If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 20/09/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Payroll-Team-Lead_R000024477-1": {
      "title": "Payroll Team Lead",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-10\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n- Salary:  $126,306– $140,543 (HEW 8) per annum, plus 17% superannuation and annual leave loading - Appointment type: Full-time, continuing role - Location: Macquarie University, Wallumattagal Campus, North Ryde Lead payroll excellence, develop a capable team, and deliver pay experiences our people can rely on. As Team Leader, Payroll Services, you will guide that team and shape the everyday experience of paying our people well. This is a hands-on leadership role where you will oversee the delivery of payroll operations and pay-related enquiry services, including compensation and benefits. You will balance operational delivery with people development, using data and insight to lift service quality, streamline processes, and uphold the governance and compliance standards our community expects. If you enjoy turning complex payroll challenges into reliable outcomes, and you find purpose in helping a team grow and perform, we would welcome your application. About the Role Reporting to the Manager, Payroll Services, you will manage the day-to-day delivery of payroll operations and pay-related enquiry services, ensuring accurate, timely and customer-focused outcomes. Your responsibilities will include: Managing the day-to-day delivery of payroll operations and pay-related enquiry services, including compensation and benefits, and escalating payroll issues promptly to key business stakeholders. Guiding, coaching and developing team members through regular feedback to help build a high-performing, customer-focused culture and grow team capability. Allocating work, managing workflow priorities and monitoring performance so service standards, deadlines and quality requirements are consistently met. Acting as the primary escalation point for complex payroll enquiries and issues, enabling timely resolution and appropriate management of risk. Ensuring compliance with payroll controls, segregation of duties, legislative requirements and approved policies, procedures and governance frameworks. Identifying and helping to implement continuous improvement initiatives, including process enhancements, system changes and service delivery improvements. Evaluating payroll, enquiry and performance data to identify trends, inform decisions and improve processes, procedures and team effectiveness. Building productive relationships with leaders and stakeholders across the organisation to address systemic challenges and manage service delivery expectations. Coordinating payroll-related audits, compliance reviews and assurance activities, and helping to implement remediation actions. Helping to develop and maintain payroll policies, procedures, standards and documentation so they remain current, effective and aligned with legislative and organisational requirements. About Us Our HR Shared Services team plays a vital part in this, delivering accurate, reliable and people-focused pay, compensation and benefits services that support staff across the University. As part of this team, you will help create a workplace where our people feel valued and well cared for. About You You are an experienced payroll professional who combines operational know-how with a genuine interest in developing people. You bring a high level of accuracy, sound judgement, and a service-focused approach, and you enjoy improving the way things work while keeping compliance and governance front of mind. Selection Criteria A relevant tertiary qualification in business, human resources, accounting, finance or a related discipline, or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Demonstrated experience managing payroll operations in a complex, high-volume environment, including payroll controls, governance requirements and risk mitigation. Sound working knowledge of payroll legislation, awards, enterprise agreements and compliance requirements. Demonstrated experience guiding, coaching and developing teams to achieve service and performance objectives. Well-developed analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to resolve complex payroll matters and use data to improve performance. Experience using complex HR/Payroll enterprise systems (experience with Dayforce APAY, Kronos, Workday, ServiceNow or Finance1 is highly regarded). Effective stakeholder management and communication skills, with a high level of attention to detail and a commitment to customer service (payroll-related certification, accreditation or professional membership is desirable). How to Apply To be considered, please apply online with your CV and a cover letter outlining how your experience aligns with the selection criteria (above). Applications Close:  Sunday 20th of September 2026 at 11:59 (AEST) We reserve the right to progress or decline an application prior to the application closing date. For enquiries, or a confidential conversation about the role please contact Kate Williams, TA Consultant – k.williams@mq.edu.au . Pre-Employment Checks  Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity. Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for.  Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University. If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 20/09/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Postdoctoral-Researcher_R000024428": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Researcher",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-09\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n• Annual base salary from $112,550- $127,138 (Level A.6 to Level B.1) p.a plus 17% employer's superannuation contribution and annual leave loading. • Full-time, fixed term role for 12 months (with possibility of extension) • Based on site at Macquarie University, Wallumattagal Campus, North Ryde Macquarie University is seeking a Postdoctoral Researcher in Mechanical/Mechatronics/Materials Engineering to join an industry-funded project on recycling end-of-life solar panels. The Role Every year, a growing number of end-of-life solar panels enter landfill. The researcher will work on a project focused on recycling end-of-life solar panels and will collaborate closely with the industry partner. The project involves delaminating solar panels, recovering constituent materials, and extracting valuable resources. This project is being undertaken with an industry partner and has the potential to significantly improve the management of electronic waste by addressing the growing number of end-of-life solar panels entering landfill. We are looking for a passionate researcher who can undertake mechanical design, design and conduct experiments, learn quickly, solve complex problems, develop innovative solutions, and contribute to both academic and industry knowledge through this project. Your key responsibilities include: Design and integrate mechanical systems Design tools and equipment for solar panel delamination Design systems for component handling and material recovery during delamination Design and set up a metal recovery system Characterise and scientifically analyse material quality Measure adhesion forces Design and conduct scientific experiments, and collect, analyse and interpret data Contribute to managing and maintaining laboratory equipment Generate and disseminate high-impact research outputs, contributing to reports, conferences and potential IP development Assist in preparing journal publications, conference presentations and grant applications Supervise and mentor higher degree research students where appropriate Collaborate with multidisciplinary teams across academia and industry Ensure compliance with laboratory safety procedures and quality standards How to Apply To be considered for this position, please submit your CV along with a separate document responding to the selection criteria below. Essential A PhD in mechanical/mechatronics/materials engineering or a closely related discipline Demonstrated track record in mechanical design and/or tool design. Demonstrated track record of research excellence with emerging or established recognition Strong interpersonal, written and verbal communication skills Commitment to teamwork and collaborative work, both domestically and internationally Desirable Previous experience in working on industry projects, with the ability to adhere to project timelines, milestones, and deliverables. *Please note that this position will require a criminal record check. We are only considering applications from candidates who are currently based in Australia and hold full working rights. Applications Close: 23 September 2026 at 11:59pm (AEST) For role enquiry, please contact Dr Binesh Puthen Veettil at binesh.puthenveettil@mq.edu.au *** Applications will be reviewed as they are received, and we reserve the right to progress or decline an application prior to the application closing date. We also reserve the right to close the advertisement early if a sufficient number of qualified applicants is received. Why Join Us? Macquarie is a university engaged with the real and often complex problems and opportunities that define our lives. Since our foundation over 60 years ago, we have aspired to be a different type of university. Over the years, we have grown to become the centre of a vibrant local and global community. Connect with us today . We rank amongst the top employers in the Australian Workplace Employers Index. Explore the fantastic benefits available to you when you become part of the team at Macquarie University. Flexible, hybrid work arrangements 17% Superannuation Subsidised onsite parking options Extensive training and professional development programs Onsite childcare facilities to support working parents Onsite vacation care during school holidays Discounted health insurance Subsidised membership at our Sport & Aquatic Centre Access to an Employee Assistance Program for free and confidential support Convenient onsite GP, imaging, and physiotherapy clinics Pre-Employment Checks Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity. Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for. Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University. If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 23/09/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Research-Data-Scientist_R000024227": {
      "title": "Research Data Scientist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-09\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAcademic Level A ($89,579 – $120,621) or Academic Level B ($127,138 - $150,425) plus 17% superannuation and annual leave loading Full-time, 3-year fixed term appointment Macquarie University, Wallumattagal Campus, North Ryde Turn complex research data into discovery and help advance global brain health. We have an exciting new opportunity for a data scientist to do work that truly matters and carries an impact. As part of the neurosciences program within the Macquarie Medical School, you'll transform complex research data into insights that shape the future of brain health. In this role, you'll shape how data is handled, analysed and processed across the neurosciences program within the Medical School, directly advancing new research programs, including new precision diagnostics for neurology and three international Aligning Science Across Parkinson's (ASAP) grants that connect clinicians, researchers and collaborators across the globe. This is a rare opportunity to apply your bioinformatics and data science capabilities to a variety of research platforms, including genomics, proteomic, transcriptomic, analysing microscopy, imaging, and clinical data, and developing the tools and pipelines that help our researchers turn complex datasets into scientific discovery and diagnostic applications. About the Role Reporting to Professor Glenda Halliday, you will be involved in the full lifecycle of research data, from collection and organisation through to analysis, visualisation and sharing. Indicative datasets include genomic, proteomic, transcriptomic, microscopy, imaging, clinical and related metadata. Your key responsibilities will include: Collecting, generating and organising source research data into structured repositories. Analysing data using existing tools and developing new analytic tools, code and processing pipelines as required. Visualising and presenting data using specialised bioinformatics tools. Setting up and configuring data processing platforms and environments at the University and with trusted external partners, including the use of containerisation for workflows and pipelines. Helping the Halliday Team and FMHHS research staff access tools and building their capability through training and advice. Contributing to research publications and outputs, including data formatting, presentation and sharing, and uploading data and code to publicly accessible repositories. Working within human research ethics approvals (HREC), the Privacy Act and the My Health Records Act, and adhering to EEO and WHS policies. About Us The Faculty of Medicine, Health and Human Sciences (FMHHS) is pushing the boundaries of progressive thinking to help address some of the big issues of our time, both nationally and on a global scale. The faculty forms part of MQ Health, an integrated academic health sciences enterprise incorporating Macquarie University Hospital and primary and speciality clinics. We have active research programs in biomedical and clinical sciences, cognitive and brain sciences, health systems, linguistics, physiotherapy, psychology and public health, and host the internationally acclaimed Australian Institute of Health Innovation (AIHI). About You You are an experienced Research Data Scientist who enjoys applying technical expertise to research problems and helping others build their own data capability. You bring secure data handling knowledge, strong bioinformatics skills, and a genuine interest in contributing to research that makes a difference. Essential Selection Criteria (Level A and Level B) A master's qualification or above, with demonstrable experience in data science supporting research programs, from data collection and analysis through to visualisation and sharing. Knowledge of secure data handling protocols and procedures, including applying institutional data sensitivities to datasets. Skills in image analysis and bioinformatics approaches, with programming ability in R, Python, and Jupyter Notebook. Experience with version control systems (Git/GitLab/GitHub) and workflow languages (e.g. Nextflow, Common Workflow Language). Experience using data processing environments and platforms (e.g. NCI, ARDC Nectar Research Cloud, JupyterLab, Neurodesk) and with machine learning (Torch/PyTorch). Clear communication and documentation skills, including the ability to document research tools, code and analytical processes, and to explain complex data concepts to researchers and collaborators across the Medical School. Familiarity with HPC platforms, containerised applications, FAIR data principles (Desirable) Selection Criteria for Level B (in Addition to the Criteria Above) A PhD or progress toward a doctoral qualification in a relevant discipline (bioinformatics, computational biology, data science, neuroscience or related. A demonstrated track record of research outputs, including peer-reviewed publications, data publications, code repositories, or equivalent demonstrated scholarly activities relevant to brain health, neurodegeneration, bioinformatics, genomics, imaging or related fields. Demonstrated ability to carry out independent research, including independently designing, developing and implementing analytical frameworks, bioinformatics pipelines and data platforms with minimal day-to-day supervision. How to Apply To be considered for this position, please apply online and attach your Resume and a separate Cover Letter outlining how you meet the selection criteria above. We kindly request that you indicate in your cover letter whether you are applying for this position at Academic Level A or Academic Level B, so the selection panel can assess your application against the relevant criteria. Applications Close Applications for this role will close on Wednesday 30th September at 11.59 PM AEST. Specific Role Enquiries For role-specific enquiries, please reach out to Professor Glenda Halliday at glenda.halliday@mq.edu.au . Why Join Us? Macquarie is a university engaged with the real and often complex problems and opportunities that define our lives. Since our foundation over 60 years ago, we have aspired to be a different type of university. Over the years, we have grown to become the centre of a vibrant local and global community. Connect with us today . We rank amongst the top employers in the Australian Workplace Employers Index. Explore the fantastic benefits available to you when you become part of the team at Macquarie University. Flexible, hybrid work arrangements 17% Superannuation Subsidised onsite parking options Extensive training and professional development programs Onsite childcare facilities to support working parents Onsite vacation care during school holidays Discounted health insurance Subsidised membership at our Sport & Aquatic Centre Access to an Employee Assistance Program for free and confidential support Convenient onsite GP, imaging, and physiotherapy clinics Pre-Employment Checks Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity. Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for. Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University. If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 30/09/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Senior-Lecturer-in-Cyber-Security_R000022247": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Senior Lecturer in Cyber Security",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-09\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSalary: Level B from $ 127,138 to $150,425 plus 17% employer's superannuation and annual leave loading  Salary: Level C from $ 155,236 to $178,523 ​ plus 17% employer's superannuation and annual leave loading Appointment Type: Full-time, continuing Location: Macquarie University, Wallumattagal Campus, North Ryde Macquarie University is seeking an outstanding academic with an excellent track record of teaching and research in Cyber Security. The position will be based in the School of Computing, Faculty of Science and Engineering with close interactions with the Macquarie University Cyber Security Hub. The successful applicant will be expected to develop, teach and convene units at the postgraduate and undergraduate levels, while supervising Higher Degree Research students as well as leading and collaborating on research projects. The successful candidate will demonstrate an excellent track record in research and teaching, as well as personal and professional skills that can enable service and leadership contributions that will help to strengthen the impact and reputation of the School of Computing, Macquarie University Cyber Security Hub, Faculty of Science and Engineering, and Macquarie University. About Us You will be joining a growing School of Computing in the Faculty of Science and Engineering with a fast-rising reputation (Top 50 globally for Computer Science and Engineering, in 2025 Shanghai Global Ranking of Academic Subjects, and Top 100 globally for Data Science and AI, in 2025 QS World University Rankings by Subject). The School of Computing is currently the home of more than 60 academic staff and over 150 research students, and close to 3,500 undergraduate and postgraduate coursework students. The school offers a broad range of cutting edge undergraduate and postgraduate courses and enjoys a strong research ethos. In Macquarie's Faculty of Science and Engineering, you'll join passionate researchers and educators blazing new trails in the spirit of discovery and exploration. Encouraged to think boldly, and supported by some of Australia's most outstanding facilities, brilliant minds converge in our faculty to create incredible new possibilities: the world's first attempt to synthesize complex life, the creation of Wi-Fi, the discovery of dancing dwarf galaxies, and the development of blue LED light. Inspired by challenge and opportunity, we look forward to welcoming you as we imagine a new future together. The Macquarie University Cyber Security Hub was established in 2016 as a strategic university initiative in partnership with industry and government. Building on an initial seven-year $12 million collaborative investment with Optus, the Hub is now widely recognised as one of Australia’s leading and globally respected cyber security research and development centres. It brings together multidisciplinary expertise across computing, data science, artificial intelligence, law, and the social sciences to address complex and emerging cyber security challenges. The Hub is home to the Information Security and Privacy Research Group, one of Australia’s premier research groups in privacy-preserving technologies, with internationally recognised contributions to data security, AI security and privacy, human-centric security, and cyber-physical systems protection. It has secured substantial competitive national and international research funding and maintains deep, sustained partnerships across government, defence, critical infrastructure, telecommunications, financial services, and global technology sectors. A defining strength of the Hub is its strong translational and industry engagement focus, leading multi-million-dollar collaborative programs that convert research excellence into deployed capability and measurable impact. This includes the development of advanced AI-driven security technologies and the creation of Apate.AI, a multi-award-winning university spin-out combating global phone scams. The Hub plays a central role in advancing cutting-edge research, shaping cyber security policy and practice, and strengthening Australia’s national and international cyber security leadership. Globally recognised as one of Australia's leading research universities, Macquarie is a university engaged with the real and often complex problems and opportunities that define our lives. Since our foundation in 1964, we have aspired to be a different type of university: one unbound by ivory towers and sandstone walls. Our campus spans 126 hectares, with open green space that gives our community the freedom to think and grow. Uniquely located in the heart of Australia’s largest high-tech precinct with more than 300 leading companies, our students can tap into industry connections that give them an edge in their future careers, while our staff have access to outstanding research and innovation opportunities with some of the world’s leading organisations. About You (Selection Criteria) You are an accomplished academic and researcher with deep expertise in cyber security, a commitment to excellence in teaching, and the interpersonal skills to thrive in a collaborative, multidisciplinary environment. You bring a strong track record of impactful research, meaningful industry engagement, and a genuine passion for mentoring the next generation of researchers and practitioners. A PhD in cyber security or a closely related discipline such as Computer Science, computer networking, or distributed systems. Demonstrated publications in top-tier peer-reviewed journals and/or conferences in security, privacy, data mining, AI, machine learning, or computer networks. Demonstrated research leadership, success, and impact in high-quality cyber security research, aligned with the school’s areas of excellence (privacy-preserving technologies, human-centric security, AI security and privacy, and cyber-physical systems security and privacy). Demonstrated success in teaching cyber security at undergraduate and postgraduate levels, including the ability to develop scholarly and innovative approaches to teaching and learning. Demonstrated ability in attracting nationally competitive and/or industry research funding. A strong record of supervising Higher Degree Research students, particularly PhD level students. A solid track record of effective teamwork, engagement with external stakeholders (particularly cyber security stakeholders) and contribution to the academic life and administration of a university or professional setting. How to Apply: To be considered for this position, please submit: Your curriculum vitae; A cover letter outlining your interest in the position; and A statement addressing how your experience and achievements align with the relevant selection criteria. Applications Close Applications will close on Wednesday 7th October at 11 PM AEST. Enquiries For enquiries, or a confidential conversation about the role, please contact Professor Amin Beheshti at amin.beheshti@mq.edu.au . Why Join Us? Macquarie is a university engaged with the real and often complex problems and opportunities that define our lives. Since our foundation over 60 years ago, we have aspired to be a different type of university. Over the years, we have grown to become the centre of a vibrant local and global community. Connect with us today . We rank amongst the top employers in the Australian Workplace Employers Index, having recently earned a five-star rating in the QS World Rankings with the highest rating for employability. Take a look at the fabulous staff benefits on offer when you work at Macquarie University: Flexible, hybrid work arrangements 17% Superannuation Subsidised onsite parking options Extensive training and professional development programs Onsite childcare facilities to support working parents Onsite vacation care during school holidays Discounted health insurance Subsidised membership at our Sport & Aquatic Centre Access to an Employee Assistance Program for free and confidential support Convenient onsite GP, imaging, and physiotherapy clinics Pre-Employment Checks Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity. Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for. Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University. This role may require a Defence Trade Controls Act 2012 section 10A permit (10A Defence Control Permit), and appointment will be subject to satisfying all requirements associated with that permit. If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 07/10/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Hotel-Front-Desk-Night-Auditor_R000024426": {
      "title": "Hotel Front Desk Night Auditor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-07\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nKeep our hotel's front desk running smoothly through the night, deliver memorable guest experiences and grow your hospitality career - Salary package: $67,500 per annum plus 12% superannuation. - Appointment type: Full-time (37.5 hours per week), continuing position. - Lakeside Hotel & Conference Centre, Macquarie University, Wallumattagal Campus, North Ryde. About the Role We currently have an exciting opportunity for a f ull-time Hotel Front Desk Night Auditor to join our Hotel and Conference team. This is a great opportunity to work within a capable, close-knit team and develop your career in the hospitality industry. Reporting directly to the Front Office Manager, the Night Auditor is a key member of the hotel team responsible for the overnight operations of the hotel from 11:00 p.m. to 7:00 a.m., with shifts commencing Sunday to Thursday. Combining front-desk service with essential night-audit activities, you will support guests throughout the night, verify the accuracy of guest accounts, and reconcile and balance charges. Key responsibilities include: Performing hotel guest check-in and check-out Settling accounts for early departures Addressing customer queries and resolving customer issues, and completing the necessary reconciliation and reports Conducting walkthroughs of the building to ensure it is secure, and reporting any maintenance issues Working alongside relevant stakeholders to deliver on shared outcomes ​ If you take pride in creating and delivering memorable guest experiences, we welcome your application. The successful candidate will ideally commence as soon as possible. About Us MGSM Hotel and Conference Centre is an award-winning venue situated on the picturesque grounds of Macquarie University at North Ryde. The hotel and conference centre facilities include hotel accommodation, an à la carte restaurant, a café, and multipurpose meeting and event spaces. Benefits of working at Lakeside Hotel & Conference Centre Conveniently located on Macquarie University’s parkland campus, Lakeside Hotel & Conference Centre is within walking distance of Macquarie University Metro Station and Macquarie Centre. Our employee benefits include: Complimentary Macquarie University Sport & Aquatic Centre gym access Bonus discounts and reward points at Campus Life operated hospitality and retail outlets Ongoing development and mentoring opportunities Generous leave entitlements, including paid parental leave Access to our staff wellbeing program and staff support services Working on a vibrant parkland campus, with a wide variety of food and beverage outlets, and general practice and hospital amenities Access to discounted corporate health insurance and a complimentary employee flu shot program ​ About You You have a positive attitude, a genuine customer service focus, and the technical ability to process the nightly audit of all front office transactions. Comfortable working autonomously through overnight shifts, you enjoy solving problems as they arise and take pride in delivering memorable guest experiences. Selection Criteria Demonstrated skill and experience within a customer facing role providing excellent service to a culturally diverse customer base, Experience in customer billing and invoice processing, Excellent attention to detail, Availability and capability to work autonomously across overnight shifts Strong time management and organisational skills, A calm, service-focused approach to resolving guest queries and issues, and Experience using hotel management systems (e.g., Opera) is desirable. *** This position requires a Criminal History Check, and applicants must hold a current First Aid Certificate. How to Apply To be considered, please apply online with your CV and a cover letter outlining how your experience aligns with the selection criteria (above). Applicants must hold valid Australian work rights and be able to maintain those rights on an ongoing basis for this continuing appointment. Applications Close: Monday 21 September 2026 at 11:59 p.m. (AEST) We reserve the right to progress or decline an application prior to the application closing date. For enquiries about the role, please contact Saad Khan at s.khan@mq.edu.au . Pre-Employment Checks Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity. Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for. Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University. If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 21/09/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Head--Employee-Relations_R000024475-1": {
      "title": "Head, Employee Relations",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-07\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nLead the University Group's employee and industrial relations function, providing strategic direction and oversight of complex workplace relations matters, enterprise agreement bargaining and implementation, employment policies, and union relationships. Package Circa $240K including up to 17% superannuation negotiable Full time, continuing appointment Macquarie University, Wallumattagal Campus, North Ryde Provide strategic oversight of employee relations across a leading University group Macquarie University is seeking a Head, Employee Relations to provide strategic oversight of our employee and industrial relations function across the University Group, including Macquarie University, Macquarie University Hospital and our controlled entities. In this senior role, you will guide the University Group through complex workplace matters, enterprise agreement implementation and bargaining, and union relationships. You will help ensure our people management practices are fair, effective and aligned with legislative obligations, while contributing to a high-performing, collaborative and respectful workplace culture. This is an opportunity to make a meaningful contribution at scale, partnering across Human Resources and the wider University to help realise our strategic objectives and enhance the working lives of our academic and professional community. About the Role Reporting to the Chief People Officer and leading a team of Senior Employee Relations Consultants and a Health Management Advisor, you will: Oversee the provision of high-quality employee relations advice and services to key stakeholders, particularly in relation to complex cases, dispute resolution and matters under the University Group's Enterprise Agreements and awards, ensuring processes are managed fairly and in line with legislative and procedural requirements. Guide a whole-of-HR approach to managing complex matters, from conduct and performance to significant change management projects, including effective case management, elevation and intervention. Oversee the implementation of the University Group's Enterprise Agreements and Awards and provide significant input into the planning and negotiation of enterprise agreements across a range of industrial contexts. Provide coaching, professional guidance and mentoring to ER and HR team members and identify capability-building opportunities to enhance individual and team performance. Develop and maintain productive relationships with unions to promote industrial harmony and effective workplace relations solutions. Represent the University and its controlled entities in meetings and negotiations with unions, and in employment-related legal proceedings where required. Take a lead role in the development, maintenance and review of HR policy, particularly policies with an employment and industrial relations element. Actively participate in the HR Leadership Team, model expected behaviours, and help shape a positive workplace culture, while ensuring compliance with relevant EEO and WHS obligations. About Us Human Resources provides advice and services to the University and its controlled entities (including Macquarie University Hospital) across the attraction, selection, performance, development and remuneration of our workforce, and ensures compliance with relevant workforce legislation. Employee Relations is a specialist HR team responsible for advising on the development and implementation of industrial instruments, complex case management of complaints and matters relating to performance, conduct and workplace change, and liaison with unions on industrial issues. The team works in close consultation with HR Business Partners, HR Shared Services, and specialist teams across Capability, Culture and Inclusion and Talent Acquisition to deliver responsive, high-quality service. About You (Selection Criteria) You are a seasoned employee and industrial relations practitioner with deep knowledge of the employment legal framework and a track record of guiding organisations through complex workplace matters. You bring sound judgement, clear communication and a genuine commitment to fair and effective people practices. HR, IR or legal qualifications and related experience. Deep understanding of the employment-related legal framework and principles. Demonstrated experience overseeing complex case management, dispute resolution and change management processes. Experience contributing to enterprise agreement bargaining and implementation across varied industrial contexts. Proven capability in mentoring and developing team members and building organisational capability. Experience developing and maintaining effective relationships with unions and a broad range of stakeholders. Strong experience in and understanding of risk management practices. Experience working within the Higher Education context would be highly regarded. How to Apply To be considered, please apply online with your CV and a cover letter outlining how your experience aligns with the selection criteria (above). Applications Close: Wednesday 23 September 2026. We reserve the right to progress or decline an application prior to the application closing date. For enquiries, or a confidential conversation about the role please contact David Ward, Chief People Officer at d.ward@mq.edu.au or Sarah Bate, Head of Talent Acquisition at sarah.bate@mq.edu.au or Kate Williams, Talent Acquisition Consultant at k.williams@mq.edu.au . Why Join Us? Macquarie is a university engaged with the real and often complex problems and opportunities that define our lives. Since our foundation over 60 years ago, we have aspired to be a different type of university. Over the years, we have grown to become the centre of a vibrant local and global community. Connect with us today . We rank amongst the top employers in the Australian Workplace Employers Index. Explore the fantastic benefits available to you when you become part of the team at Macquarie University. Flexible, hybrid work arrangements 17% Superannuation Subsidised onsite parking options Extensive training and professional development programs Onsite childcare facilities to support working parents Onsite vacation care during school holidays Discounted health insurance Subsidised membership at our Sport & Aquatic Centre Access to an Employee Assistance Program for free and confidential support Convenient onsite GP, imaging, and physiotherapy clinics Pre-Employment Checks Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity. Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for. Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University. This position requires a Criminal History Check and Qualification Check. If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 23/09/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Director--Graduate-Futures_R000024399-1": {
      "title": "Director, Graduate Futures",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-07\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nLead the Graduate Futures team providing programs and support to students across employability, career readiness and global mobility. Attractive senior contract negotiable including 17% superannuation Full-time, 5 year appointment (renewable) Macquarie University, Wallumattagal Campus, North Ryde Shape graduate futures, build meaningful partnerships and create impact at scale Macquarie University is seeking an outstanding leader to join us as Director, Graduate Futures within the Pro Vice-Chancellor Education (PVCE) portfolio. This is a rare opportunity to play a pivotal role in shaping how Macquarie students transition from university into the world of work - locally, nationally, and globally. Reporting to the Pro Vice-Chancellor Education, you will provide strategic and operational leadership across student employability, career readiness, and global mobility, helping to ensure that every Macquarie graduate is equipped to thrive in workplaces increasingly shaped by artificial intelligence and emerging technologies. You will guide the University-wide implementation of the Future Ready transdisciplinary unit, oversee inbound and outbound student exchange programs, and build the partnerships and platforms that position Macquarie as a partner of choice for producing work-ready, future-focused graduates. This is a position for someone who is energised by impact, collaboration, and innovation at scale. If you are motivated by helping students build the skills, literacies and adaptability they need to succeed in a rapidly changing world, we would like to hear from you. About the Role The Director, Graduate Futures provides strategic and operational leadership in the advancement of student employability, career readiness, and global mobility across all student cohorts and faculties. Partnering closely with faculty stakeholders, industry partners, and exchange organisations, you will help ensure that work integrated learning, global experience, and employability preparedness are accessible, impactful, and coherent across the full student lifecycle. Key responsibilities include: Strategic Leadership: Provide visionary, best-practice guidance and strategic direction for the Graduate Futures function, keeping its programs aligned with the University's broader goals — including its commitments to graduate employability, AI-readiness, and student mobility. Future Ready Implementation: Guide the University-wide implementation of the transdisciplinary Future Ready unit across all undergraduate courses, partnering with faculty education leaders, curriculum teams, and the broader PVCE portfolio to enable consistent, high-quality, and scalable delivery. AI-Ready Graduates: Work with faculty partners and industry to help graduates navigate, critically evaluate, and effectively use AI tools in professional contexts, and to prepare them for labour market transitions driven by automation and technological change. Corporate and Industry Engagement: Foster a culture of partner stewardship, represent Macquarie in relevant industry forums, and act as a credible institutional voice on graduate capability and the future of work. Student Exchange and Global Mobility: Provide strategic oversight of inbound and outbound student exchange programs, keeping these well-integrated with broader employability and curriculum strategies and accessible to diverse student cohorts. Impact and Evaluation: Measure, analyse, and assess the real-world impact of programs and services on graduate outcomes, using evidence to inform continuous improvement and responsiveness to employer and market needs. People Leadership: Guide, mentor, develop, and motivate a team of approximately 25–30 staff to deliver high-quality, accessible, and valued programs, and to help build a collaborative, high-achieving culture. About Us The Deputy Vice-Chancellor (Academic) is the Chief Academic Officer of the University and holds overall responsibility for the planning, quality, and delivery of education to Macquarie's undergraduate and postgraduate students. The PVCE provides senior leadership in developing and implementing strategies that advance educational excellence, student access, widening participation, academic success, graduate outcomes, and the Macquarie University College. You will be joining a dynamic portfolio at the heart of Macquarie's academic mission, partnering with Faculty education leaders, industry and exchange partners, Student Services teams, and a range of internal and external stakeholders. About You (Selection Criteria) You are a strategic, commercially aware, and people-centred leader with deep expertise in graduate employability, careers, work integrated learning, and/or global mobility. You bring a well-developed understanding of the future of work, including the impact of AI and emerging technologies on graduate skills demand, and you are skilled at translating that understanding into programs that genuinely improve outcomes for students. A degree and postgraduate qualifications (or equivalent) in a relevant field. Demonstrated experience in the leadership and management of student-facing functions in higher education , or substantial relevant industry experience in careers, employability, or global education. Proven record of delivering high-impact programs in careers and employability, work integrated learning, curriculum-embedded employability, and/or student mobility. Demonstrated experience guiding large-scale, University- wide curriculum or program implementation initiatives , including the ability to engage and influence diverse academic and professional stakeholders. Expert knowledge of emerging social, economic, and technological trends relating to employment, the future of work, and graduate outcomes — including the impact of AI and automation on skills demand. Demonstrated success in building external relationships , with the ability to translate employer insights and market intelligence into responsive program and curriculum innovation. Excellent communication skills and the ability to build credibility and engage at senior levels with academics, professional staff, industry partners, and regulatory bodies. A sound understanding of the Australian higher education regulatory framework (including TEQSA standards) and a global perspective on student exchange, mobility, and international education partnerships. How to Apply To be considered, please apply online with your CV and a cover letter outlining how your experience aligns with the selection criteria (above). Applications Close: 23 September 2026 We reserve the right to progress or decline an application prior to the application closing date. For enquiries, or a confidential conversation about the role please contact Taryn Jones, Pro Vice-Chancellor Education at taryn.jones@mq.edu.au or Sarah Bate, Head of Talent Acquisition at sarah.bate@mq.edu.au . Why Join Us? Macquarie is a university engaged with the real and often complex problems and opportunities that define our lives. Since our foundation over 60 years ago, we have aspired to be a different type of university. Over the years, we have grown to become the centre of a vibrant local and global community. Connect with us today . We rank amongst the top employers in the Australian Workplace Employers Index. Explore the fantastic benefits available to you when you become part of the team at Macquarie University. Flexible, hybrid work arrangements 17% Superannuation Subsidised onsite parking options Extensive training and professional development programs Onsite childcare facilities to support working parents Onsite vacation care during school holidays Discounted health insurance Subsidised membership at our Sport & Aquatic Centre Access to an Employee Assistance Program for free and confidential support Convenient onsite GP, imaging, and physiotherapy clinics Pre-Employment Checks Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity. Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for. Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University. If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 23/09/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Casual-Hotel-Front-Office-Receptionist_R000024425": {
      "title": "Casual Hotel Front Office Receptionist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-07\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nEngage guests warmly, handle enquiries, support service teams, and manage efficient check‑ins and check‑outs. ABOUT YOU You are someone who believes the core of hospitality is customer service and you are a true follower of the same cause. Being an honest, reliable, and confident person, you know how to handle multiple tasks at the same time and are able to do so with a friendly, warm personality. Desired Criteria Understanding of the hotel and hospitality sectors. Strong communication, interpersonal, and conflict resolution skills. Well-presented with keen attention to detail and cultural sensitivity/awareness. Strong time management and problem-solving skills. Proficient in the use of the Microsoft Office Suite of programs and knowledge of Opera Property Management System. Previous front office, customer service and/or sales experience in a hotel environment. Demonstrated customer complaints management/resolution experience. Demonstrated experience building and managing relationships with a variety of stakeholders Cash handling and transaction processing experience. Flexible to work AM, PM and Night when required This role requires successful applicants to undergo a Criminal History Check and must have the right to work in Australia. ABOUT US Lakeside Hotel and Conference Centre, an award-winning venue situated on the picturesque grounds of Macquarie University at North Ryde, is seeking enthusiastic and customer focused Front Desk Receptionist to join or Hotel Team. The 40 Room hotel offers A la carte restaurant, café and impressive conference and event facilities featuring state of the art technology. Lakeside employees enjoy access to extensive Macquarie University facilities including a high-tech library, private teaching hospital, gym and pools, a campus train station and Macquarie Centre shopping complex next door. Benefits of Working for Lakeside Hotel & conference Centre Flexible working hours Training provided 25% off purchases at all Campus Life operated outlets Fun and collaborative values-driven culture Full access to the university's library (borrowing, printing, and data bases) Gym access If you are passionate and experienced in customer service, want to work in a fun, friendly and fast paced environment, apply now to start ASAP! How to Apply To be considered for this position, you will need to demonstrate the above requirements in your CV and Cover Letter. If you need any support or reasonable adjustments through this recruitment process, please let us know so we can provide the support you need. If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 20/09/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Graduate-Research-Liaison-Officer_R000024380": {
      "title": "Graduate Research Liaison Officer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-07\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nHelp shape an exceptional research journey and bring your organisational talent to a team that powers graduate research success. • Salary Package: $88,670 - $100,815 per annum (HEW 5), plus 17% superannuation and annual leave loading (pro-rata for part-time appointments) • Appointment Type: Part-time (0.6 FTE/ 21 hours per week), continuing position • Macquarie University, Wallumattagal Campus, North Ryde Are you an organised, people-focused professional who enjoys keeping the moving parts of a busy team running smoothly? The Graduate Research Academy (GRA) is looking for a Graduate Research Liaison Officer to provide high-quality administrative and coordination assistance to our Liaison Team. Sitting within the portfolio of the Deputy Vice-Chancellor (Research), the GRA is a central unit that provides leadership, operations and administration for our graduate research students, supervisors and faculties. The Liaison Team acts as the business partnering link between the GRA and faculties and you will be right at the heart of that connection. This is a rewarding opportunity to contribute to the experience of graduate researchers and academic staff, refine your coordination skills, and grow your career within a values-driven university that genuinely invests in its people. About the Role Reporting to the Director, Graduate Research Services and Governance, you will provide practical administrative assistance that keeps workshops, events, records and communications on track. Your day-to-day will include: Providing administrative assistance for graduate research workshops, functions, projects, activities and event logistics, including room bookings, catering and material preparation. Monitoring, maintaining and updating graduate research content across webpages, social media and learning platforms. Maintaining graduate research records, including tracking timely completion of student milestones (such as confirmation of candidature and progress reviews) and reviewing data for accuracy and reporting. Coordinating communications with graduate research students, supervisors and other stakeholders. Contributing to the design, development and implementation of improvements to administrative systems, processes and procedures. Monitoring group inboxes, responding to general enquiries and escalating where needed. Maintaining a working knowledge of graduate rules, policies, procedures and regulatory requirements, and applying these to provide advice to students and staff. Assisting in the preparation of meeting agendas, and taking and distributing minutes. About Us Macquarie is a university engaged with the real and often complex problems and opportunities that define our lives. Since our foundation in 1964, we have aspired to be a different type of university. Over the years, we have grown to become the centre of a vibrant local and global community. Connect with us today .   Within the portfolio of the Deputy Vice-Chancellor (Research), the Graduate Research Academy (GRA) provides leadership, support, operations and administration for the University’s graduate research students, supervisors and faculties. Led by the Pro Vice-Chancellor, Graduate Research, the GRA works in partnership with faculties to provide students with an exceptional graduate research training experience. The Liaison Team provides the key business-partnering connection between the GRA and the faculties, supporting effective collaboration and the delivery of high-quality graduate research services. About You You are a proactive and adaptable administrator who takes pride in accuracy, service and getting things done. You enjoy building positive working relationships, juggling multiple priorities, and using sound judgement to keep things moving in a busy environment. Selection Criteria A degree in a relevant field, or an equivalent combination of relevant experience and/or education/training. Demonstrated ability to work productively in a fast-paced environment, while also using initiative and working autonomously to manage a range of demands. Excellent interpersonal, verbal and written communication skills, including the ability to engage professionally and thoughtfully with people from diverse backgrounds. Ability to build and maintain effective working relationships with key internal and external stakeholders. Excellent time-management skills, with a demonstrated ability to respond to changing priorities, manage multiple tasks and meet deadlines using judgement and initiative. Excellent computing skills, including a sound working knowledge of the Microsoft suite and well-developed word processing and spreadsheet data-entry skills. Note: The successful candidate will also be required to complete a police check prior to commencement. *** Applicants must hold valid Australian work rights and be able to maintain those rights on an ongoing basis for this continuing appointment. How to Apply To be considered, please apply online with your CV and a cover letter outlining how your experience meets the selection criteria (above). Applications Close: Sunday 20 September 2026 at 11:59 p.m. (AEST) We reserve the right to progress or decline an application prior to the application closing date. We also reserve the right to close the advertisement early if a sufficient number of qualified applicants is received. For enquiries about the role, please contact Catherine Murphy, Director, Graduate Research Services and Governance at catherine.schedlich@mq.edu.au Why work at Macquarie We rank amongst the top employers in the Australian Workplace Employers Index, having recently earned a five-star rating in the QS World Rankings with the highest rating for employability. Our prime location is just a short walk from Macquarie University Metro Station and Macquarie Shopping Centre. Enjoy the benefits of working at a campus that offers: 17% Superannuation Subsidised onsite parking options Flexible working options Training and professional development Onsite childcare facilities Discounted health insurance (Medibank) Onsite vacation care Employee Assistance Program Subsidised membership at the Sport & Aquatic Centre Onsite GP, imaging & physio clinics Pre-Employment Checks Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity. Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for. Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University. If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 20/09/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Lecturer-in-Biology-and-Environmental-Sciences--Teaching-and-Leadership-_R000021841-1": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Environmental Sciences (Teaching and Leadership)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-07\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n- Salary Package: $127,138 - $136,453 (Level B.1 – B.3) - plus 17% superannuation and annual leave loading - Full-time, continuing appointment - Macquarie University, Wallumattagal Campus, North Ryde The role We are seeking a highly motivated and skilled Teaching and Leadership academic in Environmental Sciences to contribute to teaching, curriculum development, and governance within the School of Natural Sciences. This role provides the opportunity to deliver high-quality teaching across undergraduate and postgraduate programs, engage meaningfully with students, and contribute to the School’s teaching mission in environmental sciences. The successful candidate will bring a strong understanding of how Earth science principles lead to understand, manage, and solve environmental problems affecting the natural and built environment, more particularly in the key areas of geomorphology , earth surface processes, physical geography, earth surface observation, and/or earth surface responses to anthropogenic disturbance and hydro-climate extremes. The applicant may also have experience in environmental management in rivers, wetlands, coastal or urban environments, and/or contaminated site assessment , with the capacity to teach in these areas at third-year and post-graduate levels. The successful applicant will also have expertise in curriculum design, teaching innovation, and course planning. They will also contribute to academic governance processes, including curriculum review, accreditation, and quality assurance, while supporting and mentoring academic teaching teams. Some of your key responsibilities include: Some teaching experience in undergraduate and/or postgraduate units or courses in Environmental Sciences, including tutoring, demonstrating, lecturing and/or assessment. Demonstrated understanding of pedagogy and curriculum and contribution to unit design, renewal, and enhancement of teaching practice. Demonstrated experience contributing to course planning, academic governance, and quality assurance processes, including assessment design and moderation processes. Support program-level curriculum reform, accreditation, and continuous improvement initiatives. Demonstrated collaborative skills, including the ability to work effectively within teaching teams, engage with mentoring from senior colleagues, and contribute effectively to committees or working parties. Evidence of disciplinary discovery and scholarship, and the capacity to contribute to supervision of postgraduate and HDR students (for example, supervision or co-supervision), appropriate to career stage. About You You are an experienced and collaborative academic with a strong record of leadership in teaching, curriculum design, and academic governance within Environmental Sciences. You bring demonstrated expertise in course planning, quality assurance, and program-level curriculum reform, along with the ability to mentor and support academic and sessional teaching staff. With excellent organisational, teamwork and communication skills, you contribute positively to School and Faculty committees, workload planning, and learning and teaching culture, while maintaining active engagement in disciplinary scholarship, HDR supervision, and external partnerships that enhance student learning and impact. About Us The School of Natural Sciences is a multidisciplinary and collegial environment committed to excellence in teaching, research, and student experience. We deliver innovative, research-led education across environmental, biological, Earth, spatial information and molecular sciences, and value collaboration, curiosity, and impact in everything we do. To Apply To apply for this position, please apply online by submitting your CV and a separate cover letter (no more than 2 pages) that demonstrates how you meet the following selection criteria: PhD in Environmental Sciences ( geomorphology, earth surface processes,  physical geography, earth surface observation, and/or earth surface responses to anthropogenic disturbance and hydro-climate extremes ), or a closely related discipline (or near completion). Demonstrated teaching experience in undergraduate and/or postgraduate units or courses in Environmental Sciences. Demonstrated understanding of pedagogy and curriculum and unit design, renewal, and teaching innovation. Demonstrated experience in course planning, academic governance, and quality assurance processes, including assessment design and moderation. Demonstrated leadership, team management, and collaboration skills, including the ability to coordinate teaching teams, mentor academic and sessional staff, and contribute effectively to committees. Evidence of disciplinary discovery and scholarship, and the capacity to supervise postgraduate and HDR students, appropriate to career stage. *This position requires a criminal history and qualifications check. Role-specific Enquiries: Fleur Ponton – Head of School (Natural Sciences) - fleur.ponton@mq.edu.au . Applications Close:  Sunday 27th of September 2026 at 11:59pm (AEST) The Faculty of Science and Engineering at Macquarie University has a goal to increase the engagement of women, Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people from diverse backgrounds in STEMM roles. Applications are considered holistically, and candidates are encouraged to apply even if their experience does not meet each individual selection criterion. Pre-Employment Checks  Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity. Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for.  Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 27/09/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Manager--Orientation-and-Graduations_R000024383": {
      "title": "Manager, Orientation and Graduations",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n• Annual base salary from $126,306 - $140,543 plus 17% superannuation and annual leave loading • Appointment type: Full time, Fixed-term contract until 31 January 2028 • Based at Macquarie University, Wallumattagal campus, North Ryde We are seeking an experienced and self-motivated leader to manage the University's orientation and graduation functions and drive the development of innovative programs that enhance student engagement, belonging, and success. About the role The role provides strategic leadership and operational oversight of major student events, ensuring a high-quality experience for students from commencement through to graduation. Key Accountabilities Manage the efficient and effective delivery of conferral of awards, orientation and graduation ceremonies enhancing student experience and showcasing the University. Coordinate, at an institutional level, the delivery of student orientation and transition programs including O-Week and student induction. Lead the development of key student engagement and retention campaigns to support orientation programs and student transition initiatives at the University. Manage the delivery of successful on-campus, off-campus and overseas graduation ceremonies. Oversee conferral of awards ensuring that all aspects of the process are compliant. Undertake projects in relation to the improvement of orientation, graduation and major student events and maintain effective and efficient planning processes. Coordinate the collection and analysis of and evaluate and report on issues related to graduation and major student events, student engagement services and processes and optimising student engagement and participation. Provide expert advice to students and key internal stakeholders on the policies, systems and processes related to orientation, graduation and major student events About you You’ll be a self-starting individual with excellent work organisation and time management skills and ability to remain resilient when under pressure. You will have expert planning, design and content development capabilities, able to effectively communicate with stakeholders at all levels. You will enjoy working in a dynamic environment, applying a methodical and consultative approach in your work, and be motivated to deliver work outputs that are of a consistent high quality.   How to apply To be considered for this position, please apply online and attach your resume and a separate cover letter that outlines how you meet the selection criteria below: Degree or equivalent experience in business, education, finance, law or related discipline. Knowledge of tertiary students and the Australian higher education system. Expert knowledge of policies, processes and best practice relating to student engagement, transition and support within the higher education sector. Extensive experience in designing, leading and successfully implementing major student events and engagement initiatives, involving diverse stakeholders. Excellent organisational, planning and project management skills, with the ability to manage peak periods, competing priorities and multiple concurrent programs High level written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to prepare clear documentation, communications and reports foe senior executives. Ability to build and manage partnerships with key internal and external stakeholders.       Applications Close: 20th September 2026 at 11:59pm (AEST)   Please note we reserve the right to progress or decline an application as well as close the advertisement prior to the stated closing date. Why Join Us? Macquarie is a university engaged with the real and often complex problems and opportunities that define our lives. Since our foundation over 60 years ago, we have aspired to be a different type of university. Over the years, we have grown to become the centre of a vibrant local and global community. Connect with us today . We rank amongst the top employers in the Australian Workplace Employers Index. Explore the fantastic benefits available to you when you become part of the team at 17% Superannuation Subsidised onsite parking options Extensive training and professional development programs Onsite childcare facilities to support working parents Onsite vacation care during school holidays Discounted health insurance Subsidised membership at our Sport & Aquatic Centre Access to an Employee Assistance Program for free and confidential support Convenient onsite GP, imaging, and physiotherapy clinics Pre-Employment Checks Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity. Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for. Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University. If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 20/09/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
