    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Postdoctoral-Researcher-in-Animal-Behaviour_R000024473": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Researcher in Animal Behaviour",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-15\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\n· Salary package: $112,550 - $120,621 (HEW A.6-A.8/ PhD awarded rate) plus 17% superannuation & annual leave loading · Full-time, fixed term appointment until April 2028 · Macquarie University, Wallumattagal Campus, North Ryde The Role An exciting opportunity for a Postdoctoral Researcher exists in the School of Natural Sciences at Macquarie University. We are seeking a qualified candidate to join a team with an international reputation for producing high-quality research outcomes in the area of animal behaviour. This project involves establishing and imaging butterfly courtship interactions within experimental enclosures with the ultimate aim of reconstructing the visual circumstances leading up to mate detection. The successful candidate will contribute to an Australian Research Council funded project seeking to determine how visual parameters are used to detect target stimuli under challenging visual conditions. Reporting to the project CI (A/Prof Darrell Kemp), the Postdoctoral Researcher will: Establish the experimental arena and associated infrastructure. Undertake fieldwork in tropical North Queensland. Perform and image behavioural presentations. Extract and analyse 3-dimensional object tracking data. Lead the preparation of high impact scientific publications. We look forward to hearing from applicants who have demonstrated excellence in their past research, possess the technical skills required to match the demands of this project. Candidates with experience working with butterfly behaviour in either field or laboratory settings are strongly preferred for this position. About Us The Faculty of Science and Engineering is a young and dynamic faculty driven by the spirit of discovery. Here we nurture the next generation of science and technology innovators. From a handful of students on the University’s first day, the Faculty now serves over 8,000 students across all our courses. The School of Natural Sciences at Macquarie University was established on 1 January 2022 through the amalgamation of the Departments of Biological Sciences, Molecular Sciences, and Earth and Environmental Sciences. The School is the largest in the Faculty of Science and Engineering and is a vibrant community of educators, researchers and students working across a wide range of biological, biomolecular, biomedical, chemical, environmental and geoscience disciplines. Selection Criteria To be considered for this position, applicants must address the selection criteria below and attach their CV (including a list of two referees), a statement of research interests and achievements. Essential A PhD in animal ecology/behaviour or a related discipline. Experience working with butterflies in either field and/or laboratory environments. Ability to undertake and publish original experimental research, as evidenced by impactful and high-quality outputs. Ability to foster a nurturing environment for research students including the provision of research student supervision. Demonstrated capacity to work independently and as part of a team. Excellent oral and written communication skills. Ability for analytical thinking and independent problem solving. Desirable Experience with imaging insect interactions and the analysis thereof using tracker software. *This position requires a criminal history and qualifications check. Enquiries: Associate Professor Darrell Kemp at darrell.kemp@mq.edu.au Applications Close: Tuesday 29 September 2026 at 11:59 p.m. (AEST) *** Candidates must have valid Australian work rights for the duration of the appointment. The Faculty of Science and Engineering at Macquarie University has a goal to increase the engagement of women, Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people from diverse backgrounds in STEMM roles. Applications are considered holistically, and candidates are encouraged to apply even if their experience does not meet each individual selection criterion. Pre-Employment Checks Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity. Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for. Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 29/09/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Associate-Lecturer-in-Psychology--Teaching-_R000024523": {
      "title": "Associate Lecturer in Psychology (Teaching)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-15\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\n. Salary Package : Associate Lecturer (Level A) from $89,579 -$120,621 per annum (FTE), plus 17% employer's superannuation and annual leave loading Appointment Type: Fixed-term appointment until 31 December 2028, with flexible employment options from 0.4 FTE (part-time) to 1.0 FTE (full-time). Up to four full-time equivalent positions are available Location: Macquarie University, Wallumattagal Campus, North Ryde A wonderful opportunity to bring your teaching expertise to life, enrich the student experience and help shape the next generation of practitioners. The School of Psychological Sciences, within the Faculty of Medicine, Health and Human Sciences (FMHHS), is welcoming applications from qualified academics to help shape and deliver our accredited undergraduate and postgraduate Psychology courses. These teaching-focused positions offer the chance to focus fully on what you love, high-quality teaching, with all workload allocation dedicated to teaching duties. Joining our School at an exciting time of curriculum growth and renewal, you will play a meaningful part in developing new units and enriching the student experience across one of the largest and most highly regarded psychology courses in the country. Whether you are seeking a fractionated arrangement to balance other commitments or a fuller workload, these roles offer genuine flexibility, with designated workdays agreed each calendar year. If you are passionate about teaching applied psychology and helping students build the skills that shape professional practice, we would be glad to hear from you. About the Role As an Associate Lecturer (Level A, Teaching Focused), you will be involved in unit development and the delivery of teaching across our accredited Psychology courses. Your responsibilities will include: Contributing to unit development and teaching within accredited undergraduate and postgraduate Psychology courses. Delivering and managing teaching content, lectures, tutorials and assessments across face-to-face and/or online modalities. Teaching in applied psychology areas, including psychological assessment, counselling and/or therapy skills, and developmental, social and health psychology. Helping to create an engaging and inclusive learning experience for undergraduate and postgraduate cohorts. Being available for the role on designated workdays agreed each calendar year (for fractionated appointments). About Us The School of Psychological Sciences is ranked among the top 75 Psychology Departments in the world and is at the forefront of research, teaching and community engagement. We offer accredited undergraduate and postgraduate programs in Psychology, with the largest suite of postgraduate programs in New South Wales. The school sits within the Faculty of Medicine, Health and Human Sciences (FMHHS), whose education suite includes clinical science, physiotherapy, medicine, exercise and sports science, public health, psychology, cognitive sciences, linguistics, audiology and speech pathology. The faculty forms part of MQ Health, an integrated academic health sciences enterprise incorporating Macquarie University Hospital and primary and speciality clinics. We foster a values-based culture of innovation and creativity to achieve excellence in teaching and to enhance the research performance of the University. We invest in developing the careers and wellbeing of our students and staff, and we live our values of Caring, Integrity, Teamwork, Ambition, Innovation and Engagement. About You You are an experienced psychology educator who enjoys creating an excellent learning experience and helping students succeed. You bring recent teaching experience, relevant qualifications and a genuine interest in applied psychology teaching. Selection Criteria Completion of, at minimum, an accredited Bachelor’s degree in psychology with Honours. Preference will be given to applicants who have also completed or are near completion of an accredited Master’s coursework degree in Clinical Psychology, Clinical Neuropsychology, Organisational Psychology, Professional Psychology or Counselling Psychology. Recent experience (within the past 2 years) as a tutor in psychology units and/or contributing to lectures and workshops in accredited psychology courses in Australia. Demonstrated evidence of creating an excellent student experience and engagement with undergraduate and/or postgraduate psychology cohorts. A commitment and capability to deliver high-quality learning and teaching, including the delivery and management of teaching content, lectures, tutorials and/or assessments in face-to-face and/or online modalities. Demonstrated interest in teaching applied undergraduate and postgraduate psychology units, particularly in psychological assessment, counselling and/or therapy skills, developmental, social and health psychology. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to relate to staff and students from all backgrounds, build an inclusive teaching and learning environment, and work effectively within a team. For a minimum of 3 FTE positions: completion of an accredited master’s coursework degree in Clinical Psychology, Clinical Neuropsychology, Organisational Psychology, Professional Psychology or Counselling Psychology, and current registration as a Psychologist with AHPRA. How to Apply To be considered, please apply online with your CV and a separate cover letter (3-page maximum) outlining how you meet each of the selection criteria (above). Please note that applications for this position are only being accepted from Australian citizens, permanent residents, and those currently residing in Australia with full working rights. Applications Close : Monday 5th October, 2026 at 11.55 PM AEST. Enquiries: For enquiries, or a confidential conversation about the role, please contact Professor Maria Kangas, Head of School of Psychological Sciences at maria.kangas@mq.edu.au . Why Join Us? Macquarie is a university engaged with the real and often complex problems and opportunities that define our lives. Since our foundation over 60 years ago, we have aspired to be a different type of university. Over the years, we have grown to become the centre of a vibrant local and global community. Connect with us today . We rank amongst the top employers in the Australian Workplace Employers Index, having recently earned a five-star rating in the QS World Rankings with the highest rating for employability. Take a look at the fabulous staff benefits on offer when you work at Macquarie University: Flexible, hybrid work arrangements 17% Superannuation Subsidised onsite parking options Extensive training and professional development programs Onsite childcare facilities to support working parents Onsite vacation care during school holidays Discounted health insurance Subsidised membership at our Sport & Aquatic Centre Access to an Employee Assistance Program for free and confidential support Convenient onsite GP, imaging, and physiotherapy clinics Pre-Employment Checks Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity. Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for. Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University. If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 05/10/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Research-Fellow----Photo--electrochemical-catalysis_R000024515": {
      "title": "Research Fellow - (Photo)electrochemical Catalysis",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-16\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nAdvance photoelectrochemical catalysis for sunlight-driven green fuels — from catalyst design to working prototype. · Salary package: $112,741 per annum (Level A.6, PhD awarded rate) plus 17% superannuation and annual leave loading · Full-time, fixed term 12-month appointment · Macquarie University, Wallumattagal Campus, North Ryde We are seeking a highly motivated Research Fellow to join an interdisciplinary research group at Macquarie University focused on green hydrogen, electrocatalysis and sunlight-driven photoelectrochemical fuel production. The group has established an advanced research platform for electrochemical and photoelectrochemical energy conversion, including electrochemical workstations, a solar simulator, an Incident Photon-to-Current Efficiency (IPCE) measurement system and a customised roll-to-roll magnetron sputtering facility. Researchers also have access to advanced characterisation capabilities and external synchrotron and photovoltaic facilities through national and industry collaborators. Current research directions include AI- and data-driven discovery of multielement catalysts, amorphous catalyst structure–activity relationships, water and seawater electrolysis, and integrated solar-to-fuel systems. The Role Working closely with Dr Doudou Zhang, Professor Vladimir Strezov and a growing network of national, international and industry collaborators, the Research Fellow will develop next-generation catalysts and integrated devices for renewable-fuel production. This position is particularly suited to an emerging researcher seeking to build a strong independent research profile through high-quality publications, new research concepts, competitive grant applications, HDR supervision, and industry and international collaboration. Key responsibilities include: Design, synthesise and optimise electrocatalysts and photoelectrochemical materials for hydrogen and sustainable fuel production. Conduct electrochemical and photoelectrochemical measurements, including CV, LSV, EIS, stability testing, product analysis and solar-to-fuel/device performance evaluation. Fabricate and optimise catalyst electrodes and devices, with opportunities to use scalable roll-to-roll magnetron sputtering fabrication. Undertake advanced materials characterisation and collaborate with national and international partners on specialised in-situ/operando and synchrotron characterisation. Analyse and interpret experimental data, establish composition–structure–property relationships, and contribute to mechanistic understanding of catalytic processes. Prepare high-quality journal publications, technical reports and conference presentations, and communicate research outcomes to academic and industry partners. Contribute to competitive research grant applications and the development of new collaborative research projects. Support and co-supervise HDR and undergraduate research students, providing guidance on experimental design, laboratory practice, data analysis and scientific writing. Work collaboratively across multidisciplinary teams and contribute to the safe and effective operation of laboratory facilities. Engage with external research institutions and industry partners and contribute to the translation and scale-up of promising renewable-energy technologies. About Us Macquarie is a university engaged with the real and often complex problems and opportunities that define our lives. Since our foundation in 1964, we have aspired to be a different type of university. Over the years, we have grown to become the centre of a vibrant local and global community.   Connect with us today . The   Faculty of Science and Engineering   is a young and dynamic faculty driven by the spirit of discovery. Here we nurture the next generation of science and technology innovators. From a handful of students on the University’s first day, the faculty now serves over 8,000 students across all our courses. Within the faculty, the School of Engineering brings together researchers and educators across electronics, mechanical and mechatronic, civil, software and sustainable energy engineering. Our work is applied and outward facing, with active partnerships across industry, government and the research sector, and access to well-equipped fabrication, electrochemistry and materials characterisation facilities. This role sits within our energy and materials research activity, alongside colleagues working on renewable energy systems, advanced materials and device engineering, and contributes to government-funded programs including those coordinated through ARENA. You will be part of a research community that values careful experimental work, open exchange of ideas and research that reaches beyond the university. About you (Selection Criteria) A PhD in Materials Science, Chemical Engineering, Chemistry, Electrochemistry, photovoltaic or a closely related discipline. Demonstrated research experience in one or more relevant areas, including electrocatalysis, photoelectrochemistry, water electrolysis, green hydrogen, solar fuels, or electrochemical energy conversion. Strong hands-on experimental skills in electrochemical and/or photoelectrochemical characterisation, including techniques such as CV, LSV, EIS, Tafel analysis, stability testing, IPCE, and solar-simulator measurements. Experience in the synthesis and optimisation of catalysts, functional materials, electrodes, or photoelectrodes, with the ability to independently design and conduct experiments. Experience with relevant materials characterisation techniques, such as XRD, SEM/TEM, XPS, Raman, spectroscopy, or related methods, and the ability to interpret structure–property–performance relationships. Demonstrated ability to analyse complex experimental data, troubleshoot research problems, maintain high-quality research records, and work independently while contributing effectively within a multidisciplinary team. A strong research track record relative to opportunity, demonstrated through peer-reviewed publications, conference presentations, or other relevant research outputs. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to prepare high-quality manuscripts, technical reports and research presentations. Demonstrated commitment to laboratory safety, research integrity, collegiality and an inclusive research environment. *This position requires a criminal history and qualifications check. How to Apply To be considered, please apply online with your CV and a cover letter outlining how your experience meets the selection criteria (above). Role Enquiries: Dr. Doudou Zhang at doudou.zhang@mq.edu.au . Applications Close:   Wednesday 30 September 2026 at 11:59 p.m. (AEST) *** We reserve the right to progress or decline an application prior to the application closing date. Please note: Candidates must have valid Australian work rights for the duration of the appointment. The Faculty of Science and Engineering at Macquarie University has a goal to increase the engagement of women, Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people from diverse backgrounds in STEMM roles. Applications are considered holistically, and candidates are encouraged to apply even if their experience does not meet each individual selection criterion. Pre-Employment Checks  Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity. Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for.  Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University.  Why Join Us? We rank amongst the top employers in the Australian Workplace Employers Index. Explore the fantastic benefits available to you when you become part of the team at Macquarie University. Our prime location is just a short walk from Macquarie University Metro Station and Macquarie Shopping Centre. Enjoy the benefits of working at a campus that offers: 17% Superannuation Subsidised onsite parking options Flexible working options Training and professional development Onsite childcare facilities Discounted health insurance (Medibank) Onsite vacation care Employee Assistance Program Subsidised membership at the Sport & Aquatic Centre Onsite GP, imaging & physio clinics If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 30/09/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Postdoctoral-Research-Associate_R000024494": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-16\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\n- Salary package: $112,550 - $120,621 (A.6-A.8) per annum, plus 17% employer's superannuation contribution and annual leave loading. - Full-time, one-year fixed term role - Based at Macquarie University, Wallumattagal Campus, North Ryde The Role We are seeking a highly motivated and skilled research associate to contribute to a discovery project on photoelectrochemical ammonia synthesis funded by the Australian Research Council The successful candidate should have research experience in electrochemical technology and prototype design. They will have excellent oral and written communication skills and ability to work in a team collaborating across disciplines. About You You will be an emerging researcher with strong experimental capability and demonstrated expertise in spectroscopy, electrochemistry, and device prototyping. You enjoy hands‑on laboratory work, iterative troubleshooting, and mentoring junior researchers. You are collaborative, organised, and committed to producing high‑quality scientific outcomes. About Us The School of Engineering  sits within the Faculty of Science and Engineering and is a diverse community of academics blazing new trails in the spirit of discovery, exploration and impact.  We are talented and knowledgeable engineers and form teams of innovators and creators with a passion for a strong desire to make an impact in research. To Apply To apply for this position, please apply online by submitting your CV and a separate cover letter (no more than 2 pages) that demonstrates how you meet the following selection criteria: PhD in Materials Engineering, Chemical Engineering, or a related discipline Demonstrated research expertise in electrochemical systems, electrocatalysis, or device prototyping Role-specific Enquiries: Professor Yijiao Jiang, yijiao.jiang@mq.edu.au Applications Close: Thursday, 15th October 2026 at 11:59pm (AEST) *** International applicants are encouraged to apply, visa sponsorship available for the successful candidate, subject to eligibility. The Faculty of Science and Engineering at Macquarie University has a goal to increase the engagement of women, Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people from diverse backgrounds in STEMM roles. Applications are considered holistically, and candidates are encouraged to apply even if their experience does not meet each individual selection criterion. Why work at Macquarie   We rank amongst the top employers in the Australian Workplace Employers Index, having recently earned a five-star rating in the QS World Rankings with the highest rating for employability.     Our prime location, we are walking distance from Macquarie University Metro Station and Macquarie Shopping Centre.  Not only are we close, take a look at our benefits on offer:     17% Superannuation     Subsidised onsite parking options    Flexible working options    Training and professional development    Onsite childcare facilities    Discounted health insurance (Medibank)    Onsite vacation care    Employee Assistance Program    Subsidised membership at the Sport & Aquatic Centre   Onsite GP, imaging & physio clinics   Pre-Employment Checks Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity. Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for.  Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University.  If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 15/10/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    }
